{"ok":true,"document":{"ok":true,"generatedAt":"2026-11-13T02:40:56.794Z","taskKind":"network","limit":100,"policy":{"visibility":"directory_public_discoverable_operator_tasks","taskDetail":"hive_task_detail_url_only_for_network_project_tasks","privateEvidence":"excluded"},"totals":{"tasks":100,"rewardActualPft":13385},"tasks":[{"taskId":"task_bb658f1f3997a890db53882a91a0d846","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Unbounded MCP Buffering in CorbanuTerminal","description":"Show with a runnable test how CorbanuTerminal can consume excessive memory while connecting to a malicious or broken MCP server, and land that proof in a merged pull request. An MCP server is a separate program that provides tools to the terminal; codex-rmcp-client is the component that connects to it. Bug report CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal #1946 says its HTTP connection code reads an older-format response without a size limit during the initial connection, so a server can keep sending data until the host runs out of memory. Deliver a reproduction packet containing a local test server, exact run commands, memory measurements against a bounded control, and the affected file and function in codex-rmcp-client. A narrowly scoped fix is welcome but optional; do not change unrelated connection behavior.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_4f9ca4b90fd518bd1a76c82a9d748090","lastEvent":{"txHash":"D4995D4E550DDA9624C7722C1B96C82E5BECBF0E86278E318ABD6D4052EC7DFB","cid":"QmUS7347MFy9yzHDfdzxeKnnQV6qBEBbC3qay2X4tJJbUB","occurredAt":"2026-11-10T02:19:42.630Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_bb658f1f3997a890db53882a91a0d846","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_bd476da23113abd0cec3cd0da621c2d4","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce settle_agent Early Return and Merge Regression Fix","description":"CorbanuTerminal can report a spawned agent as settled before that agent’s turn has actually finished; your goal is to prove this timing gap and land regression coverage, with a small fix if needed, in the main branch. CorbanuTerminal is the Rust project at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Bug report #1894 says that in core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_tests.rs—the tests for running multiple agents—the settle_agent helper can return when an agent enters Errored state even though its turn is still active. The reported trigger is a 401 authentication response caused by the test dummy API key. The turn may emit TurnComplete or TurnAborted, the events showing that it finished or was stopped, only after settle_agent has already returned. Confirm this behavior from the code and a targeted test or trace rather than assuming the report is correct. Payment requires a new pull request from the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account, merged into main after this task was created. An open, draft, closed, unmerged, or previously rewarded pull request does not qualify.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_20d3f785688886055bc2df392f5a4de4","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B16AC4BBCC1BCD2C770273DA16A9C1491D79790301F31BAE242417472FF4AC7F","cid":"QmUyuM49GswnVccrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-11-10T02:19:08.230Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_bd476da23113abd0cec3cd0da621c2d4","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_49e67804ecc5da712d1d753b376b24ec","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Package One PostFiat L1 Edge Case","description":"PostFiat L1 v2 needs a repeatable demonstration of one boundary where the node accepts or rejects a valid transaction incorrectly, or computes or applies a result inconsistently. The finished work is a merged pull request to postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2, the PostFiat L1 v2 node repository, containing a small reproduction packet that another developer can run—not just a written report.\n\nChoose behavior that has not already been reported or paid for. Do not reuse the earlier investigations of RPC release_limit clamping, window-cap rounding, refusal-order documentation, or the doc-comment CI fix. Use valid inputs, explain the expected result using repository code or documentation, and capture the different actual result. Include a similar control case that behaves correctly. Keep this PR limited to the reproduction; do not change consensus rules or bundle in a fix.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_fb264c5e3e750178463496a6eed985a3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"81D32DDEB9E6A69BB3B0461114413A8EFD242CE0C4EABA092E1F0F1B18C41AEA","cid":"Qma11fByoHqU8kKKewrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-11-09T15:02:11.128Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_49e67804ecc5da712d1d753b376b24ec","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_57d39a74d51c61aaa6115fc5ce00b53f","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Benchmark Untested CorbanuTerminal Classifier Input Patterns","description":"The goal is to find shell input patterns that make CorbanuTerminal’s command-safety classifier slow down disproportionately, and to deliver a merged GitHub pull request containing a repeatable timing script and clear results. CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal is the GitHub repository, and the classifier checks whether shell commands are safe to run. Merged PR #1804 on 8 November 2026 fixed scaling problems for repeated environment assignments, repeated here-documents, and repeated leading write redirects. This task probes different input forms that fix did not cover; it does not require changing the classifier itself. For each pattern, state whether doubling the input roughly doubles run time (linear) or makes it grow faster (super-linear).","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_18ecc0c0a4087cc9c83423dbe469ab54","lastEvent":{"txHash":"CE8CCB11A38C72850211356E6D50C36351EA75AA4F1C9AE0F2F86A135D1970A1","cid":"QmS4XyE2LwaKi3Gp8kxsNmhuBeyk6DJxQAY68gWnvaKMBn","occurredAt":"2026-11-09T11:10:21.938Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_57d39a74d51c61aaa6115fc5ce00b53f","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_37ce64c6abb899ba109dbfcf17617c7d","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Test ext:: Git Remotes Against CorbanuTerminal Classifier","description":"Find out whether CorbanuTerminal’s safety classifier catches dangerous Git ext:: remotes and, if it finds a bypass, land a small fix. In Git, an ext:: remote can run a command on the user’s computer, so it must not slip through unmarked. GitHub issue #1876 asks whether launcher input or saved Git settings can introduce these remotes without a dangerous verdict. Test both routes on current main and provide exact, repeatable proof. Payment requires a pull request authored by your linked GitHub account and merged into main after this task was created; an open, draft, closed, or previously paid pull request does not qualify.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d3e57120eb2e62378d0bc0944657b1a3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B06945B8A20163C90945DC075FED4DEB87E756EB9AC9C56095165DDE020543BE","cid":"QmcmoXNDTN7ek4TSzM5vtWR2kcGkJzdiMYG4k1hQPFSNNH","occurredAt":"2026-11-09T03:32:52.754Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_37ce64c6abb899ba109dbfcf17617c7d","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4352b74ed1e0cf84234709a2b55eab98","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Classifier Walk Misreads With Tests","description":"CorbanuTerminal sometimes classifies valid shell commands incorrectly; reproduce the reported failures, fix the command-reading code, and land a merged pull request with regression tests. Bug report #1845 at https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/1845 describes two failures in the classifier walk, the code that reads a command to decide how to classify it: commands starting with redirections and short zsh loops using [[ ]] are misread. The fix must match shell behavior and keep the existing tainted_action tests, which check classification of potentially risky commands, passing.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_4c19d249cace5a081db113b678adeb85","lastEvent":{"txHash":"399C8700F8A8B252B46DC481D36A03DE9FF2B027676C6DB53AA7C79B47F19FC6","cid":"QmSZKjNopVusnJmXnEQWfDGmbhzRhRxJeu7fekdEHVWJrh","occurredAt":"2026-11-09T02:07:46.030Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4352b74ed1e0cf84234709a2b55eab98","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_28378a85b6c4bcb845061068857ee562","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix CorbanuTerminal’s Flaky Proxy Test","description":"Make a CorbanuTerminal network-proxy test stop failing at random, and land the fix in the repository’s main branch. Bug report #1883 in CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal concerns the test http_connect_accept_blocks_hooked_host_in_full_mode_without_mitm_state. The test checks that a watched (“hooked”) host is rejected by the allowlist when the proxy is in full mode but has no state for intercepting encrypted traffic. Instead, repeated runs can produce either blocked-by-allowlist or blocked-by-mitm-required, indicating a race in how the proxy chooses the block reason. Work on Linux using the current main branch. Payment requires a non-draft pull request authored by your Task Node-linked GitHub account and merged into CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal main after this task was created. An open, closed, unmerged, or draft pull request does not qualify, and a pull request already paid for another task cannot be reused.","rewardActualPft":300,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5c5f87aaa1b47df42280b50c7fe720e3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B09029B19FE33AAAD251C2DEF909A5115692B7BBE678D62815027346F390CCCD","cid":"QmV6ayymZf9nq7uYAgzHVDjHVDWVvvtGgknYtp8QmvhXpQ","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T23:34:15.591Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_28378a85b6c4bcb845061068857ee562","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_c2bc3b734e98cee2b6c8c6dfe7ffd113","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Classifier Slow Input Handling","description":"CorbanuTerminal’s command classifier can become much slower than it should on certain inputs; finish with a merged Rust fix and regression tests that keep those cases fast. Bug report #1774 (https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/1774) describes running time that grows much faster than input size for environment assignments such as A1=1 through A<n>=1, long runs of <<E markers, and long runs of >a redirects. It follows earlier classifier work in issue #1719, so read that report for context. The fix must be platform-independent and preserve the classifier’s existing safety behavior. Payment requires a new PR from your linked GitHub account that is merged into the repository’s main branch after this task is created.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_1669eb242819f4cc4d465bc83b47d870","lastEvent":{"txHash":"7BF6AF3CC4BF95F497F231CC5E6462D5F4DA5FD36425C324751B97E2F7473BD1","cid":"QmS4zvMKTNgLjML7GQqKVsqrpMYMF5Zv3D2LBTx86tQoJv","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T20:50:09.166Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_c2bc3b734e98cee2b6c8c6dfe7ffd113","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_c65bb41d6e7e47a9af75d3fac2b21ce5","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix Security Classifier Auto-Approval Bypass","description":"CorbanuTerminal’s security classifier decides whether a command is dangerous enough to require user confirmation; your goal is to find one dangerous command that it wrongly auto-approves, prove the bypass with a test, fix it, and get the fix merged. Work against current main of CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, using /home/pfrpc/repos/CorbanuTerminal if that checkout is available. Possible shapes include git options before the subcommand, such as git -c k=v push; dashed helper programs launched through Windows cmd /c or mixed-case absolute paths; and redirection forms not already covered by existing regression tests. A valid finding must demonstrate a real dangerous command that auto-approves on unmodified main, not merely a test failure or a command that already prompts. Payment requires a new PR authored by your linked GitHub account and merged into main after this task was created. Open, draft, closed, unmerged, or previously paid PRs do not qualify.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_a11546047a58e0937ff1c88c854d1ef5","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4EABECF18807AB85CAD1C450054621042ED6B8E2A2A7D8BA6E54E1B3181DE5DD","cid":"QmaS9sP5zVsdR3mCpNrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T20:41:58.762Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_c65bb41d6e7e47a9af75d3fac2b21ce5","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7566fc41c46d724834bba770d75007ae","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix Redirection Classifier Cases","description":"CorbanuTerminal’s command-safety checker misses some risky commands when shell redirection is used; finish with a merged pull request that reproduces every case in GitHub issue #1772 and fixes the checker. CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal is the terminal’s public repository, and issue #1772 lists the failing examples: a command hidden behind a leading redirection is judged only by its name, while quoted-space file names, repeated < or <<<, and split &> cases produce no warning on main. These are follow-ups to merged PR #1719, which fixed other classifier problems but not these redirection cases. When input is marked untrusted, or “tainted,” the classifier decides whether the terminal should ask before running a command. The required code reading is named redirect_words/unredirected: it interprets shell redirection so the checker can identify the real command and its targets.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_01ed9c2b37b8cd1bdc117e5abd959f7d","lastEvent":{"txHash":"3B471FDB9CA5E3BB7B7EE691FA51C4805EFD9042BE4AA5BE2DB125A68F2964D6","cid":"Qmbij8kSnWWWN3SYdsnRmN4KVe6M3P2o7SRuhqeLyiPySR","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T19:40:09.304Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7566fc41c46d724834bba770d75007ae","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_b582d0715327741aa095938508d9ef1f","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal sudo option parsing with tests","description":"CorbanuTerminal reads some sudo command options differently from sudo itself; the finished work is a merged pull request that fixes the reader and adds passing regression tests. The repository is https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, and bug report #1773 at https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/1773 lists the failing command lines. Its programs() helper uses the WRAPPERS table to decide whether an option consumes the following value. Reproduce every listed quiet failure on main, including -R dir (sudo's chroot option), abbreviated long options, and clusters containing unknown letters, then make the reader match sudo's behavior.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_0e79ad6ae46bbe98b7d85776d815e9d7","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B01C130D395C14DD2041959AB7F7A47FA6B5AD4A8CEF5811D2DD405603AFF62E","cid":"QmZ1jf6f8nJagZj4Y3osfDYomehMKjKJLAT6Cw8yckeAUz","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T16:46:51.043Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_b582d0715327741aa095938508d9ef1f","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4c01a7a0f9dd2f57c7e0cf8a2319fafa","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Wrapped Git Output Path Safety Prompts","description":"CorbanuTerminal currently stays silent for some wrapped Git commands that write through relative paths; the finished work is a merged fix that asks for confirmation whenever the destination cannot be proven safe. CorbanuTerminal is the app in the CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal GitHub repository. Bug report #1661 (https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/1661) lists security gaps; its item “#1606 (a wrapper's git outputs)” covers output files created by a Git command launched inside another Git command. For example, in `git -C ~/r submodule foreach git log --output=../../.zshenv`, the inner command's relative output path is not checked against the submodule's working folder. `git bisect run` has the same gap. Update the code under `codex-rs/core/src/security/`, which decides when a command needs a safety prompt, so these paths are checked against the submodule or an unknown working folder. If the destination cannot be proven safe, require a prompt. This change may only add prompts; it must not silence any prompt shown today. Add regression tests in `codex-rs/core/src/security/tainted_action_tests.rs`, the existing test file for these safety decisions. Payment requires a PR authored by your linked GitHub account, araupooo, merged into main after this task was created, plus a Discord announcement posted before submission.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5e7b368f38fa76bb7b4e7375f8ed9fe0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"7A22E9D7D35D69AD3707ADA22C41258D7D4FA0EF2D1CD1FECF316874EB18D815","cid":"QmRD2BBHEsZjN4mDiJahUptxCLzuhpBRt3ckgGj5YmRQ9u","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T15:57:49.980Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4c01a7a0f9dd2f57c7e0cf8a2319fafa","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_243a1ddbb71bde3766d03ff96c412445","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Security Prompts and Merge PR","description":"CorbanuTerminal sometimes misses dangerous Git options and therefore skips a safety prompt; finish a small fix, prove it with tests, and get your pull request merged into main. Work in the CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal repository. Issue #1528 is a security follow-up to issue #1516 and covers two gaps: Windows cmd/PowerShell checks can miss options when a dashed Git helper is called by its Windows path, and rerun::git_runs_program—the function that decides which Git commands need scrutiny—recognizes only known subcommand names, missing aliases and autocorrected names. Add prompts for these cases without removing or weakening any prompt that main already shows.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_8f3a4135efe1b04eb251403d8b182d78","lastEvent":{"txHash":"55B471B14229D84CC95FB298A035185C4C32A2C078521E1FB4978E7E5A9F73E7","cid":"QmPCnNFRtA18FBK4RZGDGVhn54AVtwzmPTev3jkrEohtcL","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T14:14:26.267Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_243a1ddbb71bde3766d03ff96c412445","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_42d36bd08f1d918180fb4fd3bc55b89f","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Git Safety Prompts and Merge","description":"CorbanuTerminal misses security warnings for two kinds of risky Git commands; finish by merging a small fix into main that adds the missing warnings without removing any existing ones. Work in the CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal repository. Bug report #1528 is a follow-up to earlier security report #1516 and describes both gaps. First, the Windows cmd/PowerShell checks inspect Git program options without identifying the subcommand, so dashed helpers launched by path, such as git-grep.exe -Osh x or git-clone.exe -u ./x u, can escape the warning. Second, rerun::git_runs_program recognizes only grep, clone, and push by name, so an existing alias such as alias.g=grep followed by git g -Osh x, or an autocorrected typo such as git gerp -Osh, is not recognized. Add prompts for these cases: read the Windows helper's subcommand, and warn on -O, -u, and --upload-pack-style options for unknown Git subcommands. This is strictly only-add-prompt work: main must never produce fewer prompts after your change.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_ae769904e26e0a974d814752b446c5c0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"59071DD79E3D4BCBA0E85B6CBF4C66C1D33464B6BC92189AB873C001307B48CB","cid":"QmYzKrREDACTED6WLsvA","occurredAt":"2026-11-08T07:17:58.284Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_42d36bd08f1d918180fb4fd3bc55b89f","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_70167211890c96d092074591d9c08ac9","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Add Adversarial Tests for CorbanuTerminal Classifier Fix","description":"CorbanuTerminal’s classifier used to consume excessive memory when it handled many long file names; the finished work is a merged pull request with stronger tests that stop this bug from returning. Bug report #1132 describes the problem in the code that prepares file-name targets for the sed text-editing command. Merged pull request #1587 fixed the blowup and added one regression test. Extend that coverage with mixed long and short file-name lists, inputs immediately below, at, and above the memory limit, and checks that unsafe or oversized input is rejected instead of processed.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_cded1884f0655af6f0bf675c24c9dbc0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"3BFAD5447EE56254956AC8BB704A061C57D100122390F192750277A15769BB0B","cid":"QmefHdQ7LMHY2k5X5GszsyctwTdMjfLkoDxrXsDFty5vB3","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T22:37:38.763Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_70167211890c96d092074591d9c08ac9","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7a6e89c51045c7d7e0e3e599d1104248","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Four Sudo Classifier Cases With Regression Tests","description":"CorbanuTerminal's command-safety classifier still misreads four sudo/eval command forms; finish by merging a fix and regression tests into CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal's main branch. GitHub issue #1482 is the bug report listing these parsing problems. Pull request #1575 fixed the first sudo option-parsing case but explicitly left items 2-5 unresolved, so this task covers only those four remaining cases. The request points to codex-rs/core/src/security/tainted_action/indirect.rs as the classifier file; confirm that path on current main because no verified commit was supplied for it. Payment requires a new pull request authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account (darkmatter-sudo) and merged into main after this task is created.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_de34fb7f609d5f4110adf42dfef36eb5","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B1DC6D8AE79A5D46499BD42A7D35D7782FAB9B2178740D52D49A5CB814026FF3","cid":"QmemaXrREDACTEDR21Tt","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T22:13:03.687Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7a6e89c51045c7d7e0e3e599d1104248","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7515c4b881e7f52597f10e8e7247c02c","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix Another Retry-Masked Flaky Test","description":"A CorbanuTerminal test listed in bug report #349 can fail on its first run and then pass when the automated test runner retries it, hiding a real bug; reproduce one such failure, fix it, and land the fix on main. Work in https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Do not use real_event_path_preserves_fifo_when_mailbox_coalesces_turns: merged PR #1603 already fixed that test. Deliver a public reproduction packet with raw before-and-after output, plus a new pull request from your Task Node-linked GitHub account that is merged into main after this task was created.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7b3abb9d02acf5b69db13beb8c86e498","lastEvent":{"txHash":"84525139C7E38A7F5251C1E92AE3179FC8E237EB674E0838DC34FE82E72F574B","cid":"QmWhR2PQomwYe79t6yMUZcs4GKyHMhtoVqwjgCNS5sHKVb","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T20:34:40.666Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7515c4b881e7f52597f10e8e7247c02c","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_5bef8d0d2030f291568b368f2f8cd1d7","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Replace Flaky Parallel Tool Test With Overlap Check","description":"Fix a flaky CorbanuTerminal test so busy Linux CI machines are judged by whether two tools actually run at the same time, not by whether a turn finishes within 1.6 seconds. Bug report #1448 at https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/1448 describes these timing failures. At main commit 1329ea58833c2bbef4fc19b4d60fb09bab52e188, the test mixed_parallel_tools_run_in_parallel in codex-rs/core/tests/suite/tool_parallelism.rs allows 1.6 seconds for tools that sleep only 300 and 250 milliseconds, so serial execution can pass while scheduling delays can make parallel execution fail. Replace that timing check with timeout-bounded synchronization that directly proves both distinct tools overlap, retains successful shell-output checks, and fails under deliberately serial execution. Keep the diff limited to this test and its supporting test helpers. Payment requires a pull request authored by your linked GitHub account and merged into CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal main after this task was created.","rewardActualPft":800,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d9eec2d3ad4cf1d7a6460e15dd82d90b","lastEvent":{"txHash":"98FDF4409FB17A917E9879D70D5031569CE2365A213337D5B9ECBB01DB871A25","cid":"QmZszCBxakxHkDMe6XugyDVmCuccNut2G47883x2iPwhMT","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T15:40:50.955Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_5bef8d0d2030f291568b368f2f8cd1d7","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a740883734050148aee1bee5d2cf36e5","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Zero Token Usage After Compaction and Rollback","description":"CorbanuTerminal sometimes reports token usage as zero when usage is actually unknown; the finished work is a merged GitHub pull request with a regression test and a fix. CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal is the terminal app's GitHub repository. Its bug report #1570 says recompute_token_usage—the function that recalculates usage after compaction (shortening conversation history) or rollback (reverting conversation state)—can emit all-zero counters even when the AI provider never supplied usage. As a result, exec --json prints a non-null turn.completed.usage full of zeros, although the release notes promise null for unknown usage.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_3c1bf799df4332f1800c1b497f2c7e12","lastEvent":{"txHash":"30D4862E9C2AA18F9644C403D94C1300A9039A21BA54C6388093CCD23D42155C","cid":"QmfNH526YVDYufEZSz62mQNCV5CdFetfFFEtmhj73wtTwW","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T14:02:52.878Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a740883734050148aee1bee5d2cf36e5","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_e613d82ca97dbe6129dca8eff526a4ff","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Git Brace Prompt False Positives","description":"CorbanuTerminal sometimes asks for a safety confirmation on a harmless git command line; ship a merged pull request that removes the false prompt without weakening the real warning. Issue 1514 is the bug report for this problem. It follows PR 1512, an earlier merged change whose safety check, called D156 in the review discussion, tracks quoted text across the whole line instead of separately for each command. For example, git add src/{a,b}.rs && git commit -m \"msg\" can prompt even though the quotation belongs to the later commit command. Narrow the quoted-text tracking to the commands that actually precede the brace word, where text such as {a,b} or {1..3} may expand into multiple arguments. Add regression coverage for both the harmless line and a case that must still prompt. Payment requires a new PR to CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and merged into main after this task is created. An open, draft, or unmerged PR is not paid, and a PR already paid for another task cannot be reused.","rewardActualPft":500,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_53505998504d31242ccc3f29936aeb22","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4D900FB09896869745EC7617A507F79B7C29CE7F0DAD14D6427315A76A8E7170","cid":"QmPg3pMYdphfLjN5woB7m5ocEn2RU376gxxUfb7MueXaYY","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T13:22:55.151Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_e613d82ca97dbe6129dca8eff526a4ff","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8269cfd54b47ca1be10ec58c8d71c801","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix zsh redirect classification and merge regression test","description":"Make CorbanuTerminal’s command safety check recognize zsh’s `=cmd` form, and finish with a merged pull request containing a regression test. Bug report #1573, item 1, explains that zsh expands `=mytool` to the installed program’s full path. Therefore, `echo x >> =mytool` appends to that program file, while the current classifier treats `=mytool` as an ordinary output filename. The project request identifies `is_safe_command.rs` as the classifier file and commit `1329ea58833c` as the starting point. Add a unit test that reproduces the problem, fix the classification without changing ordinary filename handling, and keep the existing classifier tests passing. Payment requires a new pull request authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and merged into `main` after this task is created. An open, draft, closed, unmerged, or previously paid pull request does not qualify.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9e79efc118a6be0ee55186177648a0a3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"F93AC07C0013C9A8CD95FABB42C3A70E97008961FF0FD0C499807BE1949C5690","cid":"QmbUWo5gZG25QFZ84YARaruoBEkuzuJz6Ejv8j6QLX8hJN","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T10:13:01.740Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8269cfd54b47ca1be10ec58c8d71c801","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_1f00225481cd9e66b5d2ba8a9078de0c","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Sudo Option Parsing and Add Regression Tests","description":"CorbanuTerminal’s command classifier can mistake a sudo option’s value for the command being run; reproduce the failures, fix the parser, and get the fix merged into main. Issue #1482 in CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal describes the bug: `sudo -nC 3 sh x` treats `3` as the command and never reaches `x`, while `sudo -nD sub ./run.sh` fails in the same way. The relevant code is the WRAPPERS table in the classifier’s `indirect.rs` file; this table describes how wrapper commands such as sudo handle their options. Cover both value-taking options inside short-option clusters and long options followed by a separate value.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_0a1636d83394cd11792f56424f901bcf","lastEvent":{"txHash":"6E2ABD3A7AB04F473F1229D795C3B62EBA9BB0012469B5AC413F14EF41C3A6F8","cid":"QmNUMamsVaPcf4zTHM9DhAvp6W7ayosb9A1L8nHC9JDUnQ","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T09:10:23.868Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_1f00225481cd9e66b5d2ba8a9078de0c","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8e1fa90543031a7a0572c1e78d1afe4e","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal’s Retry-Masked FIFO Test Failure","description":"Fix a rare CorbanuTerminal test failure that can disappear when CI retries, and finish with a small pull request merged into main. In github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, bug report #349 collects test failures that retries can hide. Its October 29 update names app::tests::dispatch_integration::real_event_path_preserves_fifo_when_mailbox_coalesces_turns, which checks that mailbox work keeps its first-in, first-out order when turns are combined. Two CI build records, runs 39711899895 and 40825843964, failed on their first attempt with “every mailbox task must reach a provider boundary.” The same update says 300 loaded runs passed, so the cause is not proven. Start at main commit 1329ea58833c2bbef4fc19b4d60fb09bab52e188 and inspect the test at codex-rs/tui/src/app/tests/dispatch_integration.rs:923. Reproduce the timing gap or add focused instrumentation, then make a small code or test change with deterministic regression coverage. Preserve the FIFO assertion, make the regression fail when a mailbox task is genuinely lost, and do not change unrelated mailbox behavior.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_e6814fc978c459596917f8f04af2cbd1","lastEvent":{"txHash":"54B7E45D613F7EAA04D52AFAB8758EF7EC53EA0F94EDE303B4BF53F89702C830","cid":"QmPtb3a42auYwBzHRj3LieMjHCUx3apqRJbNiDPH4TdWvw","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T07:12:44.658Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8e1fa90543031a7a0572c1e78d1afe4e","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4043c3b32e01448761fac9d60c56ad3a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Sed Copy Blowup and Add Test","description":"Fix a CorbanuTerminal bug where a crafted command can cause excessive memory copying, and prove the fix with a regression test. Bug report #1132 in CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, following earlier classifier report #1065, says the safety code that inspects flagged commands clones the shared target list for every sed operation. Each target can be a very long file name, while the current limit counts entries instead of their total size. Many long targets can therefore make copying work grow quadratically. The finished work is a pull request from your linked GitHub account, merged into main after this task is created, with a small resource-limited test that demonstrates the problem on the old code and passes with your fix.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_bfba6475e58d9ff9abccaf6686249519","lastEvent":{"txHash":"96463E6D5194440E82ABC80D9BB1AFB0B9DDB2137FA31BB53B02DC6CDCAD32AB","cid":"QmZdChwhPGiqTNrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-11-07T00:52:29.532Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4043c3b32e01448761fac9d60c56ad3a","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a114beee2b5ae8ab4a1da358358d148e","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix External Lane Zero-Cap Releases","description":"Post Fiat’s L1 code may reject every positive release from a newly created external lane when its release limit rounds down to zero atoms, the smallest indivisible units. The finished work is a merged pull request that reproduces the bug on current code, adds tests for the boundary cases, and includes a small fix if the bug still exists.\n\nGitHub issue 184 in postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2 is the bug report. The original snapshot, commit 5fc1e23741be1d4cbc351551543ddbd2e10e440c, calculates the rounded cap in crates/types/src/external_lane_types.rs lines 157–203 but checks only that reserves are positive and the basis-point value is in range. A newer main-branch snapshot, commit 264d0f6e75927bb70df31d7af5fab39bacaf964b, adds governance-controlled cap changes, so verify current behavior rather than assuming the old snapshot still matches. Payment requires a PR authored by your Task Node-linked GitHub account and merged into main after this task is created.","rewardActualPft":1000,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_1979f1dc57c894505782ba0b603f22de","lastEvent":{"txHash":"CD3670207D90B741E296647F92827382C32CF2E41034D2FFE9B6C92DFF2863F8","cid":"QmcfPRFLACMTJ1HyULjh2Vc1cdKfoz7s4jHEA9Eeqr6TJs","occurredAt":"2026-11-06T12:19:50.999Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a114beee2b5ae8ab4a1da358358d148e","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_451024ed01d319694e208196ff8849c4","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix CorbanuTerminal Zeroed Usage Totals With Regression Test","description":"CorbanuTerminal can show zero usage after streamed chats and omit subagent usage; your finished work is a small fix with a regression test merged into the repository's main branch. Work in https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, the repository for the CorbanuTerminal app. An earlier task already reproduced this defect as issue #290, where streamed chat data was dropped from usage counters and totals displayed as zero. Do not submit another diagnosis or reproduction gist: build and land the fix. Payment requires a new pull request authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and merged into main after this task was created.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7396faa012e8a8e0f41b0a19490805cd","lastEvent":{"txHash":"97760E43602B31493ED828824D4B035CB79EA31836C4BD560AACEB22D4008F80","cid":"QmV1w8yubtsYC7zVivEyUgGZVnEQnG8q1ZQweJVhaiFY16","occurredAt":"2026-11-04T15:17:28.537Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_451024ed01d319694e208196ff8849c4","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_708cc82b62f6a151001a4e5f02a8f894","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Fragile Kitty Image Test and Merge PR","description":"A CorbanuTerminal test can fail because it matches the wrong text; the finished work is a merged pull request that makes it decode and check the actual file reference. CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal is the GitHub repository containing the terminal app. Issue 1547 is the bug report for this problem. The test kitty_local_file_pet_image_uses_file_reference_without_inline_payload is meant to prove that a PNG image is referenced by its temporary file path rather than embedded in the terminal output. Its current search for the base64 fragment cG5n can accidentally match part of the encoded path, including a path containing frame.png. Replace that fragile substring check with a check that decodes the data in the Kitty image-control message and compares it with the expected file reference. Payment requires a pull request authored by your linked GitHub account and merged into main after this task is created.","rewardActualPft":400,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d35bc92cc79c36a08e0566ed3eb9e779","lastEvent":{"txHash":"99EE48E78DA730991522B50994D6DFA580A50341A24867318724A77869CE7046","cid":"QmPYNez2tQyGLnJLnayZG5tnjz5cN4vaWqGAPsEAzw27q6","occurredAt":"2026-10-30T15:48:50.320Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_708cc82b62f6a151001a4e5f02a8f894","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_ad56370aa9730a9443ed253805ed9428","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify Two Websocket Identity Cases and Submit Merged PR","description":"Two ways of signing in over a websocket connection in CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal (a terminal application on GitHub) have no automated tests, and your job is to write tests for both and get them merged into the main branch as a pull request.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f8dd39d1c7726849de372a0c6bf67edf","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4F1E2822A357D42F3E0F5C4700E3867C60A30801FD7F1001C169F51F2BD5173D","cid":"QmaAETbvw6NXMrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-10-28T20:15:58.633Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_ad56370aa9730a9443ed253805ed9428","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_5ccacd2862d905c1925471df82d0f08b","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Relative Data-Dir RPC Bug and Open PR","description":"The Post Fiat node breaks when you start it with a relative data directory, and this task is to reproduce that failure, fix it, and open a pull request with the proof.\n\nWhat you are working on: the GitHub repository postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2 holds the Post Fiat L1 blockchain node — a Rust program that runs a blockchain and serves an RPC endpoint (a local API that wallets and other programs call to read chain data and send transactions). When the node is started with a relative data directory — a path like `./node-data`, which depends on the folder you happen to run the command from — instead of an absolute one like `/home/you/node-data`, the RPC fails. The likely cause: the relative path is never turned into a full absolute path before the RPC layer opens or binds the node's state files, so the node ends up looking in the wrong place. Work from the main branch at commit b9e7fb42fdfe37d32131922280d8f88b07c06f08 — the exact code snapshot this task was written against; if main has moved on, branch from that commit.\n\nDone looks like: one pull request against main with a small, focused change — the node starts and answers RPC calls identically for relative and absolute data directories, the repository's existing tests still pass, and the PR description shows the error before your fix and the working output after it, plus a short explanation of why the bug happened. Change only the path handling; do not clean up or reorganize unrelated code.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_de9b3e0bfede826a1f0ad79e53502c41","lastEvent":{"txHash":"1CC6525C1DF44586AE3BCBDBB4B66C4F7BF558D1B1FD30172CC781CC9F518628","cid":"QmRMMkUPSQQteKqjRxCU4xWjib6RNJdsq6JCJMtUvM5GM6","occurredAt":"2026-10-28T15:00:40.215Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_5ccacd2862d905c1925471df82d0f08b","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_d3059c84ad76d60fc6e26c0cd497be87","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Run CorbanuTerminal macOS Credential Canary Probe Five Times","description":"CorbanuTerminal is a Post Fiat terminal application with a built-in safety check called the credential canary probe: it is meant to catch the app touching or storing macOS credentials when it should not. The project needs proof that this check behaves the same way every time on a known-good version of the code. Your job: check out the exact commit 78dd811d on the repository's main branch (this pins the test to one specific, reproducible version of the code so anyone can re-run it), run the canary probe five separate times from a clean state (a fresh macOS user profile or a freshly wiped config directory, so no old credentials or settings can hide a problem), and record a pass or fail plus a timestamp for each of the five runs. Then publish the full run log and an overall verdict (all five passed, or which runs failed and what happened) as a public gist or as a comment on the relevant GitHub issue. No code changes are needed for this task.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_633502e827b117981a1019758b2dd2a6","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9C73CD7DE90F7B24E6A09067EF07F9E6AFFAAB13D5745D54DE6A97A526C4F20A","cid":"QmW2nS9sSQqvUnVPn44J83ctCuf2R5VdgMnkWbnqLrZfgY","occurredAt":"2026-10-28T10:55:04.058Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_d3059c84ad76d60fc6e26c0cd497be87","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_f47752c531fde9c7309fa27fc40eda53","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Ship One Merged PR Fixing a New CorbanuTerminal Defect","description":"Goal: find one real bug in CorbanuTerminal that nobody is already fixing, repair it, and get your fix merged into the repository's main branch as one pull request.\n\nCorbanuTerminal is a Rust terminal application. Its code lives on GitHub at CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal; main (the default branch everyone ships from) is currently at commit 55ffd027. The maintainer files many bug reports each day and usually merges good fixes the same day.\n\nPick one real defect that is not already covered by an open issue, an open pull request, or a task in progress on this project's board (PF Terminal, the task list this card comes from), and that you have not already fixed for a past task here — the same fix is not paid twice. A defect means the program does something wrong on a valid input: a crash, a wrong result, a race between threads, a flaky test, or a broken piece of terminal-UI behavior. Reproduce it first, then fix it and add a regression test that fails before your change and passes after it.\n\nPayment is strict and only for the finished work: one pull request, opened after this task was created, authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account (the account you are reading this in), and merged into main. An open, unmerged, closed, or draft pull request will not be paid, and neither will a pull request that already earned payment on another task.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_c89b1b15eb80cc36ca2508c8a3e7fb4c","lastEvent":{"txHash":"03D37301EE6FCF6FE6CC4CB42629F45A2FCBD2DAE87A197F4412352BE468B6AF","cid":"QmY3bGMAxFHKY2qjRJuYc19AArTiJ6yqDSRd8rq8zVhamT","occurredAt":"2026-10-28T04:07:33.529Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_f47752c531fde9c7309fa27fc40eda53","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_ff16ec1e119f4ae459b8ce86d8b917ae","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix One Unclaimed CorbanuTerminal Defect and Deliver Merged PR","description":"Goal: pick one reported but still-unfixed bug in CorbanuTerminal, fix it, and get your fix merged into the app's main code. CorbanuTerminal is a Post Fiat terminal app; its source code lives on GitHub at CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, and \"main\" is the repository's default branch that releases are built from. Reported bugs sit in the repository's Issues tab as open issues. Choose one that nobody has claimed, fix it, and land the change as a merged pull request (a PR: a proposed code change you submit through GitHub that a maintainer accepts into main). Payment depends entirely on the PR: it must be authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account, and it must be merged into main after this task was created. An open, draft, closed, or unmerged PR will not be paid, and neither will a PR that already earned payment for a different task.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_794d98b18efc5e43607381ca4cf3eda6","lastEvent":{"txHash":"D704B6F449E182BA3EDAD090654A116204EAA6C788D865AC26D762CE73219596","cid":"QmVGVXigst98awDviCgK3jNUA2tYLpdomyBdej66g8Q6bb","occurredAt":"2026-10-28T00:44:21.632Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_ff16ec1e119f4ae459b8ce86d8b917ae","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_f59eb700951adb481c3dd3a075831ec1","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Survey PostfiatL1V2 and Publish One Reproducible Defect Analysis","description":"Find one real, reproducible defect in the Post Fiat blockchain code and publish a public write-up of it that the next fix task can be built from.\n\nPostfiatL1V2 (github.com/postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2) is the open-source code that runs the Post Fiat blockchain. The repo has open issues and fresh changes landing on its main branch, but nobody has recently checked which reported problems are still genuinely unfixed. Read the repo's open issues and its recent main-branch commits, pick ONE defect or gap you can reproduce yourself, and publish a grounded analysis that maintainers can act on.\n\nImportant: a separate task that is already underway covers finding and fixing a node bug in this repo, so pick a different problem. Before you commit to your choice, check the open issues and pull requests to make sure nobody is already fixing it.\n\nYour published analysis must include: (1) the exact commit hash of the main branch you inspected; (2) the file paths and line numbers where the problem lives; (3) step-by-step instructions a maintainer could follow to see the problem happen; and (4) a proposed fix approach described in words. Do not change any code - this task is analysis only; a separate follow-up task will do the fix.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_46c31036a58565e3ba124cc0ad1729df","lastEvent":{"txHash":"C91F324728EA242842EFF99521A1DA20B4B5623EB577AB12FA78D95DC02CA7D4","cid":"QmeFsKy8i9U3nJ4if6qKofVj4kF721TXFQoCVE6paKB4cn","occurredAt":"2026-10-27T14:36:24.701Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_f59eb700951adb481c3dd3a075831ec1","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_b14399c2b0d5be5610cc11f61f28db3d","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Stress-Test Windows Flake #1201 and Merge Fix","description":"CorbanuTerminal (the terminal app this project maintains) has a test that fails only on Windows, and we need to find out whether it is still broken on the current code. Bug report #1201 says the test 'unauthorized_recovery_uses_external_refresh_for_bearer_manager' sometimes fails because a small helper program that refreshes login tokens (it is launched through cmd.exe) gives up after waiting 10 seconds. Two earlier fixes were already merged into main: pull request #1229 kept that helper away from a test that spawns copies of itself, and pull request #1203 added logging for how long the helper waits. Even so, the bug report is still open and no open pull request claims to finish the job. Your job: run that one test many times on a Windows machine against the latest main branch, keep the exact commands and outputs, and then either fix the remaining problem and get your pull request merged, or show with a saved run log that the failure no longer happens. This task pays 100 PFT. When a fix is needed, the only paid proof is a pull request from the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account that is merged into main after this task was created. When the bug is already gone, the paid proof is a public run log (gist) saying so. Open, draft, closed, or unmerged pull requests are not paid, and a pull request that already paid another task is not paid either.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_6cf7fdb38b256b72d426e3a63d80ff7e","lastEvent":{"txHash":"F679746031F9F308F26BAECEC5300828C17377CCE205A1EFBBC78AB3DD24D17C","cid":"QmdBB8rREDACTED54cCC","occurredAt":"2026-10-27T14:36:02.917Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_b14399c2b0d5be5610cc11f61f28db3d","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8c66a7fbd958b61b2c7f75907347d3af","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify CorbanuTerminal Summary-Link Drop Defect, Publish Reproduction Gist","description":"CorbanuTerminal is Post Fiat's Rust terminal tool (repo: github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal). A bug is suspected in the code that saves links from a task summary: the claim is that any link whose text does not begin with 'http' is thrown away, and only the first five links in a summary are ever kept. Nobody has proven this with a real run yet. Your job is to build the tool at one pinned commit, run test submissions that show what really happens, and publish the evidence as a public gist.\n\nThe suspect code is at commit 78dd811d6e3718140c938ad4839968d9995fd5ac (the main branch at the time this task was written) in two places: codex-rs/cli/src/tasknode_cmd.rs lines 1480-1481 — the path a summary takes when you submit a task from the command line — and codex-rs/cli/src/tasknode_menu.rs lines 3381-3382 — the path it takes when you submit through the interactive menu. Both spots supposedly filter links the same broken way.\n\nThe finished work is a public GitHub gist that anyone can open and re-run, showing: (1) how you built the app from a clean checkout of that exact commit, (2) the exact commands you ran to submit a summary containing one URL wrapped in parentheses — for example (https://example.com/wrapped), which starts with '(' instead of 'http' — plus more than five links in total, (3) the raw terminal output and a list of the links you submitted versus the links the app actually stored, (4) the quoted suspect lines with file and line numbers, and (5) a plain statement of anything you could not test. Do not change any code and do not open a pull request — this task pays ","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_6570c375c7f593e4022e66460ea0f2d4","lastEvent":{"txHash":"CA60751B1F67002A86AB985FEA07F9A9F057258A80078B895040BFD9A5D7F636","cid":"QmTBgGbPEDRgQhoUNj7CJvxftvDzxTQCixZPfocSjedt1s","occurredAt":"2026-10-27T14:35:23.347Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8c66a7fbd958b61b2c7f75907347d3af","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7b9ed51593c3e2e64fcc66f527706a76","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix One CorbanuTerminal Bug with a Merged PR","description":"CorbanuTerminal is Post Fiat's internal terminal tool, and its GitHub repo (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) has three confirmed open bugs that no one has fixed yet. Pick ONE of these three and fix it: (1) Issue #941 — when the app refuses to run a command because it contained untrusted content, the refusal message is never shown to the user, so the command just silently fails; (2) Issue #942 — when a user clicks 'allow for this session' for an MCP tool, the approval never actually takes effect, so they get asked again every time; (3) Issue #945 — approvals for network hosts are not epoch-fenced, meaning an approval granted in one session could incorrectly carry over when it should be re-checked. The finished work is a GitHub pull request, written by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account, that is MERGED into the repo's main branch and contains both the fix and a regression test so the bug cannot quietly come back. Your PR body must include the exact steps you used to reproduce the bug before fixing it. Payment happens only after the PR is merged: an open, unmerged, closed, or draft PR will not be paid, and a PR that was already paid by another task will not be paid again.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d2a36a57aa294d964a280c01efaeee30","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4AEA3786D73447DA2007582494E960A3700FB992BB8D8F1283C87A29D653ABA4","cid":"QmWovyty9vWbMYJY1sti9ouXARyyAWWaNZYyzfZmCqD7z7","occurredAt":"2026-10-26T23:06:37.273Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7b9ed51593c3e2e64fcc66f527706a76","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_ce426056eb3784a4a0cdd4f459814b5e","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Flaky Test #349 and Merge a Fix PR","description":"Goal: a flaky test (a test that passes sometimes and fails other times) in the CorbanuTerminal project has been reported in GitHub issue #349, and it is still broken on the current main branch. This task pays for two things: proof that you made the test fail on your machine, and a pull request that fixes the test and gets merged into the main branch. An earlier task only asked for a write-up about this bug and was refused, so this time the finished work must be a real, merged code fix. Important: this task only pays if your pull request is authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and is merged into the repository's main branch after this task was created. An open, draft, or closed pull request does not count and will not be paid.","rewardActualPft":150,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_dadd7caafb5831f908e4a66461efd79a","lastEvent":{"txHash":"6FFD1AB688A4DBE4CE8D1EB8ACE04550FA225C0C198B59F6276F88206DCF94D2","cid":"QmTQwL2x3PgKNFTFRzKjGr9iHLpMckQt4Cce9Ufwe8FN6T","occurredAt":"2026-10-26T03:14:47.519Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_ce426056eb3784a4a0cdd4f459814b5e","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_889d2098cc304f580142c37084dc7e33","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Issue #997 Test Race Under Load and Deliver Merged PR","description":"Goal: a test in one of our GitHub projects fails only sometimes, and we need proof of why before anyone can fix it.\n\nThe project is CorbanuTerminal, a terminal (command-line) tool whose code is public at https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. One of its tests is named issue_621_622_interpreter_denials_are_explained_and_listed: it checks that whenever the terminal denies (refuses) a command, it also prints a short explanation of the refusal. Bug report #997 (https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/997) says that sometimes, especially when the computer is busy running several things at once, that explanation never appears. The suspected cause is a race: two pieces of code running at the same time, where a busy machine lets the wrong one win and the explanation gets skipped.\n\nThe finished work is a reproduction packet: the exact commands you ran, how many times you ran the test before it failed, the complete unedited output of that first failing run, and a short note naming the two things that race and why the explanation goes missing.\n\nPayment rule, stated up front so it cannot surprise you: this task pays only for a GitHub pull request, opened by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account, that is merged into the repository's main branch after this task was created; you submit the PR URL as your evidence. A gist, an issue comment, or an open, draft, closed, or unmerged pull request will not be paid, and a pull request that already paid another task will not pay again. You also announce the finished work in an approved Post Fiat Discord channel","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5ed6cac1fdb04b5df840d65c92e04413","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9E89EC7622FFB6FEC607822B97A36AFA1244A404DCC9BC8CA220A54489CA1743","cid":"QmWWw23FGY6xAACvBxhkYeVbowcB4WYCDjEe5LvYrwTkn9","occurredAt":"2026-10-25T20:05:03.511Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_889d2098cc304f580142c37084dc7e33","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_857ff2271e9a5238dcc0c3730f6a3c3f","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce or Refute the macOS Test Crash in CorbanuTerminal","description":"Goal: find out whether a macOS test crash in the CorbanuTerminal project is a real bug or a one-time fluke, by re-running the crashed tests five times on a Mac at the exact code version that crashed, then publishing the full logs with a clear verdict. No code changes are required.\n\nWhat happened: CorbanuTerminal is a terminal tool whose code lives on GitHub at CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. On 2026-10-22 the repo's automated test runner (GitHub Actions, which builds and tests every proposed change) was checking pull request #1365 - a proposed change that only edited documentation files - when a test process on macOS died with signal 11 (a hard memory crash, not a normal test failure; cargo, Rust's build and test tool, stopped with exit code 101). That pull request was built on the main branch at commit 1e90ae8def, and that exact code had already passed these same tests after merging, so the crash looks flaky: a failure that appears randomly, without any code change causing it. Issue #1367 in the repo is the bug report tracking this crash; it names the group of security tests that died. You can view the crashed run yourself in the repo's Actions tab under run 39847885184 (job 120066112486).\n\nYour five-run log packet is the deliverable and earns the reward on its own. Shipping a code fix is optional: if you ship one, it only counts as a pull request from the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account that is merged into the repo's main branch after this task was created. An open, closed, or draft pull request does not count, and neither does a pull request that already ear","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f0bb8f73ae36fd0ea1658de66f5bfd56","lastEvent":{"txHash":"CEFFB44396B65CB5745DB5B4673A86374699EC9EBDAA5F04C3E1D40F7FBA9A7F","cid":"QmShCnRxEQC5qUXWS2co6GAW4JhyuYKkZEkYszGcx4kZTJ","occurredAt":"2026-10-24T06:14:33.162Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_857ff2271e9a5238dcc0c3730f6a3c3f","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4b3d85671354f94f132dab6762985a0a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce CorbanuTerminal Task-Submission Attachment Bug and Publish Gist","description":"Post Fiat contributors use an app called CorbanuTerminal to accept tasks and submit their finished work. We suspect a bug in it: when you attach a file to a task submission and press submit, the saved submission may lose its reference to that file, so the attachment is gone by the time anyone reopens the submission. Your job is to build the app, prove whether this bug is real, and publish a public bug report a maintainer can act on.\n\nBuild and run the app from the repository's main branch at commit 78dd811d - that is the exact code version this test must run against. Then attach a file to a task submission, submit it, and check whether the attachment reference survives the round trip: what you attach should still be there when the submission is saved and reopened. Record the exact steps you take and what you see. If you can, trace the code that handles attachments during the submit step and name the exact place it goes wrong; if you cannot find it, say so plainly instead of guessing.\n\nDo not change any code and do not open a pull request - this task pays for the report only. Publish your findings as a public GitHub gist or as a comment on an existing issue in the CorbanuTerminal repository, and submit that link here.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_8a38283f3e09745b801c473cf1e04baf","lastEvent":{"txHash":"5DA0135777B005E1F9CEC82CF2ECC17BB9A6D63E5FD2660BC8FEBB1740FA671E","cid":"QmeVMX59YBwoykWmAXCgsHmvdbGW7daSx7S9h5D3S7a4ha","occurredAt":"2026-10-24T06:14:20.986Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4b3d85671354f94f132dab6762985a0a","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_0150a49cc49f657b73d4b924b20eb099","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce the repeated MCP approval prompt bug","description":"CorbanuTerminal is our desktop terminal app that can connect to external tool servers (called MCP servers). Bug report #942 on its GitHub tracker says: when the app runs at its 'Moderate' security level and you approve a tool that sends data by choosing 'Allow for this session', running the exact same tool call a second time should NOT ask for permission again — but a proper test requires checking whether it does, and if so, whether the app's own first reply is wrongly being treated as untrusted input that clears the saved approval. Your job is to run this exact test on a clean copy of the latest main branch and publish the results as a public GitHub gist. This is a test-and-report task only: do not change any code and do not open a pull request.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f910fa086b86841c6cf4eb4c1ca8749f","lastEvent":{"txHash":"2F208ECD7A42994F98CCD159B221B2570A42B714F8BF9D92B8379EFE63D6B31A","cid":"Qmbw3NLTETQBA89JAJxUBkZbC3hgrxL14rNAiYYKjWVVpL","occurredAt":"2026-10-24T06:13:58.945Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_0150a49cc49f657b73d4b924b20eb099","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_023d1e4d13983846fc1836ae9c5c1c54","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Fix One Retry-Masked Flaky Test from Issue #349","description":"Some of our Linux test runs are hiding real failures: when a test fails after code is merged, the CI system silently runs it again, and if it passes on the retry the whole run shows green. Issue #349 in the CorbanuTerminal repository (the CorbanuCore GitHub organization's repo for the terminal tool) lists Linux 'postmerge-ci' runs — the automatic test job GitHub runs right after a pull request is merged into the main branch — from October 7–9 where exactly this happened. Your job: run those tests yourself on Linux, catch one test failing on its first attempt, prove the retry is what hid it, and land a small pull request that stops that test from hiding failures. Payment rule: this task pays only when a pull request from the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account is merged into the repository's main branch after this task was created — an open, unmerged, closed, or draft pull request will not be paid, and neither will one that already paid another task. Submit the merged pull request URL plus your reproduction: the exact test name, the commands you ran, the raw first-attempt failure output, and a short note on why the retry was hiding it. A link to a comment you post on issue #349 with the same findings is a welcome bonus.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7927ad4c8e7c2d020d5b00d5ba6770e3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"380FD6C0B9249ABAFA5AC2931A4C930E265D7F62446D9D36778451647B47BC44","cid":"QmcVqNCxAp2yND7RuRDUSDwmYiLFLaUTc64Lgj9PvQKPoJ","occurredAt":"2026-10-23T18:58:21.346Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_023d1e4d13983846fc1836ae9c5c1c54","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_08b00674b78f14e669a88627a5d7d122","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Make the SDK turn-failure test deterministic by bounding mock errors","description":"One test in CorbanuTerminal's TypeScript SDK passes only because a 10-second timer kills it. Your job is to make that test finish in milliseconds, the same way on every run, by having the test's fake server send a limited number of errors instead of an endless stream of them.\n\nBackground: CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal on GitHub is Post Fiat's terminal tool. In the file sdk/typescript/tests/run.test.ts (this task was written against main, commit 78dd811d), the test starting at line 755 is named 'throws ThreadRunError on turn failures'. It checks that the client throws an error when a response stream keeps failing. To fake that, the test starts a tiny mock server (a helper called startResponsesTestProxy, in sdk/typescript/tests/responsesProxy.ts) and feeds it a `while (true)` loop that sends fake 'rate limit exceeded' failure messages forever. The client retries a dead stream up to 5 times by default (that limit is DEFAULT_STREAM_MAX_RETRIES=5 in codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs, with roughly 200ms delays that double each retry - confirmed in a verified QA write-up, gist bae038c6). Because the mock server never stops, the test only ends when its 10-second per-test timeout (line 774) fires. It passes by timer, not by proving the behavior, and it burns 10 seconds on every run.\n\nWhat to change: in that one test, replace the endless loop with a fixed sequence of events: send one 'responseStarted' event (the stream opens), then exactly 7 'responseFailed' events. Seven is the client's default 5 retries plus extra; put a one-line code comment saying exactly that, so future read","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9fcd6e6807b52001f507db866dbc4784","lastEvent":{"txHash":"70E739752A88AF8F3DF4D74E527A6603FF0E9045AA2C4728782D7063A68EC820","cid":"QmUDojsZw3oTjNBA5xjWqS6PJrFhaHWyQLtvQSxvrxs8bL","occurredAt":"2026-10-20T03:16:12.762Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_08b00674b78f14e669a88627a5d7d122","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8d1a559510764fec931296d6d78a5faf","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Land One Merged Pull Request Fixing a Governance Repo Defect","description":"The goal: pick one small bug, missing test, or documentation gap in one of Post Fiat's two open-source blockchain-governance repositories, fix it yourself, and get your fix merged into that repository's main branch.\n\nBackground: Post Fiat's AI Layer 1 Governance project is built on two public GitHub repositories. `postfiatd` is the node software — a fork of the XRP Ledger code that can replay and score governance activity. `dynamic-unl-scoring` is the companion tool that scores which validator nodes should be trusted. Both accept outside contributions, and small, focused fixes get merged fastest.\n\nWhat to do: browse the current main branch of either repository and find ONE concrete, self-contained problem. Good candidates: a bug you can reproduce and fix; a function with no test coverage; a broken script or config; a README section that is wrong or missing. Avoid large refactors or design changes — maintainers merge small, clearly-scoped fixes quickly.\n\nHow you get paid (read carefully): payment requires a GitHub pull request that (1) is authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account, (2) is MERGED into the repository's default branch (main) after this task was created on 2026-10-16, and (3) has not already been paid under another task. \"Merged\" means the maintainers accepted your change and it is now part of main. An open, draft, closed, or still-unreviewed pull request does NOT count and will not be paid. Submit the merged pull request URL as your evidence.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_4fe979faf5d0a58518c9f9d93f5c54df","lastEvent":{"txHash":"64703E87CDB3367405A98DEB1780148A0C449B017D599DBAFA09904126DB8953","cid":"QmX9jvxWrREDACTEDZx7","occurredAt":"2026-10-17T22:11:06.011Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8d1a559510764fec931296d6d78a5faf","project":{"id":"board_ai_l1_governance","title":"AI Layer 1 Governance","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_14dbc0accb05e1c2d21b3f965cea9274","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Repair CorbanuTerminal Remote-Executor Tests and Re-Enable Suite","description":"The CorbanuTerminal project (GitHub repo CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, a Rust/TypeScript terminal tool) has an open bug report, issue #157, saying that 47 tests covering the remote-executor feature are failing. Because they fail, the whole remote_env test suite (a named group of tests that need a real remote environment to run) has been switched off, so none of that code is being checked anymore. The goal of this task is to find out why each of the 47 tests fails, fix the underlying code or test assumptions, turn the remote_env suite back on so all 47 tests pass again, and get that fix merged into the repository's main branch. This task pays only for a merged pull request: the PR must be opened by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and must be merged into main after this task was created. An open, unmerged, closed, or draft PR will not be paid, and neither will a PR that was already paid by another task.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_20a3e70edd2ca61941c4877832f5f300","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9FBC7B1545C96819825711293F211645E705D59E9A683B18DED5826914215F77","cid":"QmYVYteN4rREDACTED2C","occurredAt":"2026-10-17T20:21:44.265Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_14dbc0accb05e1c2d21b3f965cea9274","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_e246026f80a30e649e1d20a084881382","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce CorbanuTerminal Sandbox Symlink Failure (#502)","description":"CorbanuTerminal is a Rust/TypeScript terminal tool. Issue #502 is a bug report on its Linux sandbox: the sandbox uses a tool called bwrap (bubblewrap) to run commands in isolation. The report says that if you open a workspace by its real folder path, but a file permission denial (a rule that blocks the sandbox from touching a file) is written using an absolute symlink — a shortcut like 'link' pointing to the real absolute path of a file inside the workspace — then every sandboxed command crashes with the error 'Can't create file'. The goal of this task: confirm this bug exists on the current main branch, capture the exact error, and check whether the failure is 'closed' (the sandbox blocks everything and nothing leaks out) or 'open' (some commands still run outside the restriction). Then publish what you found in a public gist so the maintainers can fix it. This is investigation only — do not change any code.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5b075a9b74d19170c8a790678b672ab8","lastEvent":{"txHash":"8B772B0E511F7337482200511D50EC1220CB4B3A6D9DA10794CE85C75CD5ED7E","cid":"QmZsxwpe3FVWtwmiK5N9kouQJcUYmCDchocosk3kd6qk2j","occurredAt":"2026-10-17T09:52:53.515Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_e246026f80a30e649e1d20a084881382","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_78f848cdce5b51fec6bb0058c2a625d0","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Confirm pakrym Timeout TODO in CorbanuTerminal and Publish Gist","description":"CorbanuTerminal (the GitHub repository CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) is an open-source codebase that the Post Fiat community reviews. Its test file sdk/typescript/tests/run.test.ts, which checks how part of the terminal's code runs, historically carried a leftover note around line 774 that reads 'TODO(pakrym): remove timeout'. A TODO is a reminder a developer (in this case, a developer named pakrym) leaves in code for later cleanup; this one sits next to a test that uses a 10-second timeout. Nobody has confirmed whether that note still exists in the repository's main branch (origin/main, the official latest code) or whether the timeout is still needed.\n\nYour job is read-only checking plus a public write-up: look at the current main branch, then publish what you find as a public gist (a shareable web page at gist.github.com) that a reviewer can independently check. Do not change any files and do not open a pull request (a proposed code change). This task pays for the verified gist, not a PR.\n\nThe gist must contain five items:\n1. The commit SHA of origin/main you inspected (the ID GitHub assigns to each version of the code; get it with `git rev-parse origin/main`).\n2. The TODO's exact current line number, plus the name of the test it sits inside (the `it('...')` line that wraps it).\n3. What that test actually checks, in a sentence or two of your own words.\n4. Why the 10-second timeout exists, based on the test's code and any nearby comments.\n5. A one-line recommendation: keep, reduce, or remove the timeout, with a one-sentence reason.\n\nIf the TODO no longer exists, publish tha","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_159adbebe2277d611ac19d4dd3a92a0c","lastEvent":{"txHash":"62FFD0A8B2E0E9AC8DE03B1586307C9FEC0A51FDB98C86D267A333005B520F7A","cid":"QmYLR3V861NrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-10-17T09:51:22.993Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_78f848cdce5b51fec6bb0058c2a625d0","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4e4f0bd06ee6e2e72e9441786fadf947","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify CorbanuTerminal test fix passes on stock Linux","description":"Run the previously failing CorbanuTerminal test on a stock Linux machine to confirm the fix works, then publish the results. CorbanuTerminal is Post Fiat's terminal app (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal). A test named pf_23_s01_code_mode_cell_results_taint_its_later_calls was failing, and an earlier QA report showed the cause was the test environment: the default test-thread stack was too small. A fix (GitHub pull request #629, merged at commit 088bd0e4) makes async test bodies run on a 32 MiB stack so no manual stack tuning is needed. The finished work is a public verification report (gist or issue comment) showing the exact commands run, the commit hash, proof that the single test passes on a default-stack Linux machine, and the pass/fail counts for the whole pf_23 test suite. Do not change any code.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7e70f1e09bbbe7d4dd5ba9f82fbda41c","lastEvent":{"txHash":"EABFFDD0C8F0B49F34762661F5929EA7DBE3603DD4307E08E1E39E604D6909A6","cid":"QmRidVbEW4XZBCo43Ec2KKqZfPRQoJ8LZXsemFhbgNYTDo","occurredAt":"2026-10-16T23:05:15.624Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4e4f0bd06ee6e2e72e9441786fadf947","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_745bf877eb617537d33e43ccfa08294a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify CorbanuTerminal pf_23 Taint Test Fix and Publish Results","description":"CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) is Post Fiat's terminal application. One of its automated tests, pf_23_s01_code_mode_cell_results_taint_its_later_calls, used to crash with a stack overflow - the program ran out of stack memory and died mid-test. Pull request #629 (a code change that is already merged into the repository's main branch) was meant to fix that crash, and this task confirms the fix really works. On a stock Linux machine (a standard Linux install with no custom patches or tweaks), you will run that one test at the current main branch, confirm whether the crash is gone, then run the wider pf_23 test group (every test whose name starts with pf_23) and record anything that still fails. The finished work is a public GitHub gist (a shareable text page on gist.github.com) or an issue comment on the CorbanuTerminal repository that shows: the exact commit hash of main you tested, the exact commands you ran, the pass/fail result of pf_23_s01_code_mode_cell_results_taint_its_later_calls, and every remaining pf_23 failure with its first failing output lines - so the maintainers can see the true state of the test suite and what still needs fixing.\n\nPayment terms set for this task: the reward pays only for a GitHub pull request authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and merged into the repository's default branch (main) after this task was created. An open, unmerged, closed, or draft pull request will not be paid, and neither will a pull request that already paid another task. Your published test report is the required evidenc","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_b1db1cbbcdee082c34d624b2fb83dba1","lastEvent":{"txHash":"2CDECE73522589FC39AA506674C36DFBB8511D72F9A9F5F005DC0197AE7AB2E2","cid":"QmaGEp3f65rREDACTEDc","occurredAt":"2026-10-16T18:54:20.829Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_745bf877eb617537d33e43ccfa08294a","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_223da5ef033fed51ee20135ea54698a7","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix MCP Tool Drop Bug in CorbanuTerminal Issue #227","description":"CorbanuTerminal is an open-source Rust/TypeScript terminal tool on GitHub (repo CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal). Bug report issue #227 in that repo says that when the terminal uses OpenAI-style Chat Completions connections or Anthropic connections, the tools registered through MCP (Model Context Protocol, a way for the terminal to plug in external tools the AI can call) get dropped — the AI model stops seeing or being able to use those tools. The finished work is a working fix: you find the exact code that registers MCP tools on those connection types, explain in plain words where it goes wrong (with file names and line numbers), change the code so tools are no longer dropped, and land the change as a merged pull request on the repository's main branch. Payment requires a merged PR authored by the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account. An open, draft, closed, or unmerged PR does not count, and neither does a PR that was already used to claim payment on another task.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f2b662dfe064f69dbcd1a67d175eaad9","lastEvent":{"txHash":"A58D14D197F40EB251B380773D684C182AB293CF7DE9F5C69586E26D9AB52C42","cid":"QmZbWToWk1XioygkQXMG7h8xBamPeFfb3Q1amL4K9vhBXd","occurredAt":"2026-10-16T12:45:23.563Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_223da5ef033fed51ee20135ea54698a7","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a658be8cd835613d6d8fea703d5935c5","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce failing CorbanuTerminal test and publish QA report","description":"CorbanuTerminal is Post Fiat's terminal application, and its source code lives at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Someone filed bug report #553 on that GitHub repository saying that a core automated test named pf_23_s01_code_mode_cell_results_taint_its_later_calls is failing on the main branch. We do not yet know for sure whether the test fails for everyone or only on that person's machine. Your goal: download the repository, run that one test yourself, and publish a short public report saying whether the failure happens for you, exactly how you ran it, and what the first sign of trouble in the output was. Do not change any code — this task is only to confirm the bug and document it, so a developer can fix it next.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7601998172c8f40ff1f444f1f48ddab8","lastEvent":{"txHash":"3518F5DD69048AADBC1BC6E0934A5346E825E26830A6306B65C3909EADF0527F","cid":"QmVf96BrREDACTEDkhJ8","occurredAt":"2026-10-16T12:45:08.350Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a658be8cd835613d6d8fea703d5935c5","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_091a2c877d312824c30fe40b58b3f0fd","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Four Failing test_setup_telegram Tests from Issue #530","description":"Issue #530 on the CorbanuTerminal GitHub repository reports that four tests named test_setup_telegram fail when run on the main branch. CorbanuTerminal is Post Fiat's terminal application; its code lives at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. The goal is to download the repo, run those four tests, and confirm whether the failures still happen — then write up what you found in a public gist or as a comment on that issue. Do not change any code. The finished deliverable is a public GitHub gist or issue #530 comment containing: the exact commands you ran, the commit hash you tested, which of the four tests passed and which failed, and the first error message for each failing test.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5b98cab093c1aa9f6004f78a6d0088a3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"5585E1BFDCDC122C3F5915B837305DDB0D708F5F60D509A47C833D8685F6EB20","cid":"QmarREDACTEDQzeq8ozd","occurredAt":"2026-10-12T14:50:18.678Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_091a2c877d312824c30fe40b58b3f0fd","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_0a02c0c9fe2a7e409fedb222a95a72a8","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Issue #498 /dev/null Sandbox Failure, Publish QA Gist","description":"CorbanuTerminal is a terminal tool built by the Post Fiat community (GitHub repository: CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, written in Rust and TypeScript). It can run its work inside a locked-down Linux sandbox so it cannot touch the rest of your computer. Bug report #498 on that repository says that in one sandbox mode — the one that mounts your entire filesystem with nothing hidden (a `bwrap --bind / /` setup; bwrap is the Linux sandboxing tool bubblewrap) and only allows internet access through a proxy — writing to /dev/null fails. /dev/null is Linux's built-in 'black hole' file that programs send throwaway output to, so when it breaks, many ordinary commands break too. The suspected cause is that the sandbox mounts the filesystem as 'nodev' (a Linux setting that disables device files like /dev/null), but nobody has confirmed this on the current code. The goal: reproduce this bug on the repository's main branch (its current official code — commit 3254a302fd at the board's last check on October 9, or newer), capture the exact failure using a fresh sandbox profile, and publish a public GitHub gist (a simple shareable text post) with the commit hash, your commands, the failure output, and what happened versus what should have happened. That gist gives the maintainers everything they need to fix the bug without guessing. This task is investigation only: no code changes and no pull request. The Board Manager (the project reviewer) will verify the gist and your Discord announcement.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_4e8d5c902f0f7149393dcb20ef8de647","lastEvent":{"txHash":"0DB61BC06ED516BAD7CB41A9E9D95B54F1EE388F07F4700364B86F3BBB579A37","cid":"QmRSdaQhTrREDACTEDtf","occurredAt":"2026-10-11T20:47:32.862Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_0a02c0c9fe2a7e409fedb222a95a72a8","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_31ca98005a9035f784c18fa76992ccc1","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Find Why /cost Counts OpenRouter Usage as Local","description":"Find and prove why the /cost command in CorbanuTerminal counts usage sent through OpenRouter as Local usage, then post the findings publicly. CorbanuTerminal is a terminal app for chatting with AI models (repo: github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal). Its /cost command shows what you've spent on AI usage, with a Local bucket for models running free on your own machine (like Ollama) and separate buckets for paid cloud providers like OpenRouter. The bug: usage you pay for through OpenRouter lands in the Local bucket instead of OpenRouter's own. Bug report #352 on that repo covers this and has two halves — your earlier findings note (public gist 8479e96ee4efc4884f4060fec121abea, from your last rewarded task) already proved the first half, where the provider name shows up wrong; this task nails down the second. The finished work is a public gist or a comment on issue #352 with a fresh run of the bug on the current main branch, screenshots of /cost for both providers, and the exact lines in the code where usage gets sorted into the wrong bucket. Investigation only: do not change any code and do not open a pull request.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7efe72ff9909118e4e4c678c0b85946f","lastEvent":{"txHash":"76B2719053F309521C83780E3593735A4050EE8DB0ED027200A80872262ED9B6","cid":"QmQC7ivkoFcvmsSsRg3DZFfAoHeokMFBgxyGWbfQsmMBkH","occurredAt":"2026-10-11T19:28:21.593Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_31ca98005a9035f784c18fa76992ccc1","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_f18c989d2f25bfb868a14efd1db17315","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Run One Flaky CorbanuTerminal Test Repeatedly and Publish Verdict Gist","description":"The CorbanuTerminal project (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) has a bug ticket — GitHub issue #349 — listing tests suspected of being 'flaky': tests that sometimes pass and sometimes fail even though the code never changed. Flaky tests make the project's automated checks untrustworthy, because a failing result no longer points to a real bug. Your job is to pick ONE test from that list, run it over and over on a clean copy of the repository, and publish a public write-up that settles whether that test is truly flaky, with the raw output of every run as proof. This task changes no code and opens no pull request: the deliverable is a public GitHub gist (a public, shareable text page on GitHub) or a comment on issue #349, plus a short announcement in the Post Fiat Discord.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_e6190a96e0fecf9b8e3487827fafffaf","lastEvent":{"txHash":"ECEE148E114B54E52B6E44C198FC615B86607A3134D21B9ABF6E804F12AAEA27","cid":"QmQa1NdRBT6cEHLsfB2Dn6m4ebZQRDq7xL7XSfuDQvQPdy","occurredAt":"2026-10-11T06:42:24.997Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_f18c989d2f25bfb868a14efd1db17315","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7704979541b05814c471e7d2c04ecc7b","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce the /cost Display Bug and Locate Its Source","description":"The terminal app CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, a Rust/TypeScript terminal tool) has an open bug report, issue #352, filed on 2026-10-09. The report says that when you run the app's /cost command, two things look wrong: rows for locally-run AI models (like Ollama on your own machine) are mislabeled as 'gpt-oss', and usage that went through the OpenRouter cloud service gets counted in the local bucket instead of its own. The finished work is a written findings packet — a public gist or a comment on issue #352 — that shows the bug happening on the current code, and names the exact files and line numbers in the code where the /cost display labels providers and sorts usage into buckets. Do not change any code and do not open a pull request; this is investigation only.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d6d3aac399b73ba0176447bcb3619c95","lastEvent":{"txHash":"F30D5ED356AADCD549290EAE82D861F0B6D50798CCE74D061DB714455B3D76DB","cid":"QmNqT92htf7JkvDLtA7jPfb7b4aoqE9pMXVRsSUGjESfiZ","occurredAt":"2026-10-10T21:37:01.059Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7704979541b05814c471e7d2c04ecc7b","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_3acb3550f960c47840c64298b9732a68","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Image-Resize-Notice Ordering Bug from Issue #52834","description":"A bug report says the CorbanuTerminal app (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, a Rust/TypeScript terminal coding assistant) prints a message tagged <image_resize_notice> in between the outputs of tools that ran in the same batch. Some strict OpenAI-compatible servers reject that ordering and the request thread gets stuck. Your job is to check whether this actually happens on a clean copy of the app's main branch and publish what you find, without changing any code. The board expects main to be at commit 4ff38e974b; record the commit ID you actually see when you clone, and note it if it differs. The finished work is a public GitHub gist or a comment on the bug report (issue #52834 on that repo) showing the exact code locations, a captured sample of the real output order, and a clear yes/no answer on whether you saw the bug.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_988d9c281b5f3fc09533d7fa1c2e0763","lastEvent":{"txHash":"ABF7059F2A5EBFA3E8F44156699179D97D49C10C89B708754570CC38FEFA62C4","cid":"QmefNtjWCvaQD9evG8RdAGEVNnfmZjfEuY1vRvhZfMCBjy","occurredAt":"2026-10-10T19:41:54.435Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_3acb3550f960c47840c64298b9732a68","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a694abf5e233851b0a4ad9184ac44710","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Issue #290 exec JSON Usage-Zero Bug","description":"CorbanuTerminal is a Rust/TypeScript terminal tool in the repo github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Bug report #290 (opened 2026-10-08) says two things are wrong with the `exec --json` command: (1) when the AI provider's response does not include usage data (token counts), the JSON output shows zeros instead of an honest 'not reported' value, and (2) usage from subagents (helper AI calls spawned during a turn) is never added into the totals. The goal of this task: on a clean copy of the code, confirm the bug actually happens and pinpoint exactly which files and lines cause it. Do NOT change any code and do NOT open a pull request. This is a read-only investigation; the deliverable is a public gist that a maintainer can use to start fixing the bug immediately.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5cf52bde4a322373f50fbbb504181149","lastEvent":{"txHash":"79354FC6CED9EDF6AAF7222E33CD41B759F5278CE3670216CA365C84FB9B2C9F","cid":"QmTGLfLG864mqSyJU4h1NsNAcriLs2tiwQCPKE129EXa5q","occurredAt":"2026-10-10T09:34:45.277Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a694abf5e233851b0a4ad9184ac44710","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_f482a2e53dd92929527b2b70bfe5b0f8","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Issue #245 Permission-Override on Clean Main","description":"CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, a Rust/TypeScript terminal tool) has an open security bug report, issue #245, filed 2026-10-07. It says that when a config denies access to a protected path (a safety feature the project calls PF-23 protected-path denials), a separate grant of additional permissions can quietly punch through that denial, one path at a time. Nobody has yet confirmed this on a clean checkout of the main branch. The finished work is a published write-up (a GitHub gist or a comment on issue #245) showing the bug reproduced, with the exact code locations, a minimal config, and captured output proving the denial gets overridden. Do not change any code and do not open a pull request - this is a reproduction and evidence task only.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_c88cb94c681f4a70bcfb7f397fc9580c","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9D59603CD18A9470F47695F6EB4958F737AA3AF343B0B279C3255B2292233647","cid":"QmQbLwbyJmauCoVoXrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-10-10T09:34:27.483Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_f482a2e53dd92929527b2b70bfe5b0f8","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4cd0670383102b68743a2d31c69c7fd9","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Issue #29 Clippy Dead-Code Error and Open PR","description":"Goal: make the Rust code checker `cargo clippy` pass on the main branch of the Post Fiat L1 v2 node code and deliver the fix as a pull request. The project lives at github.com/postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2. Its open bug report, Issue #29, says that on a clean copy of main at commit b9e7fb42fdfe37d32131922280d8f88b07c06f08 (the exact version of main where the bug was confirmed), running `cargo clippy` fails with a dead_code error pointing at a function named `validate_asset_orchard_swap_pricing_against_ledger` — a helper that checks swap pricing against the ledger but is never called anywhere in the code. An earlier QA task already proved this failure happens exactly as reported, so this task is the fix itself, not another report. Done means: a small, focused pull request against main, linked to Issue #29, where the full clippy run is clean and all existing tests still pass.","rewardActualPft":250,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5519e5a4537670a76872b88e1cce48d9","lastEvent":{"txHash":"1D0EEF89CE309E881511099A90BCDC7733FF5B88733747709DA4107D7F9E1D10","cid":"QmNX8ztRqrREDACTEDun","occurredAt":"2026-10-07T11:01:40.268Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4cd0670383102b68743a2d31c69c7fd9","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_0ac924499fc40cf8f4bc25524d6cec99","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Claude Plan Recovery Bug and Post Packet on Issue #121","description":"Goal: show exactly how a reported bug in the CorbanuTerminal app happens, so the maintainers can fix it. CorbanuTerminal is a terminal app for AI coding agents (GitHub repo: CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, written in Rust and TypeScript). Bug report #121 in that repo says that on version v0.1.41, when the Claude Plan recovery flow runs (the app trying to resume an interrupted Claude plan), the app instead drops you back on the Providers picker screen and the pane you were working in becomes unusable. Your job is NOT to fix the code. Your job is to reproduce the bug yourself on the current main branch and post a public, checkable evidence packet as a comment on GitHub issue #121. The packet must include: the exact commit you tested, every command you ran, your installed versions (e.g., Rust/cargo), screenshots of what you saw, a short expected-vs-actual comparison, and the file paths and function names in the repo that appear to handle the recovery return. No pull request or code change is required or expected for payment.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9f6916a9811dbffe8468887ca6e04af2","lastEvent":{"txHash":"55D52E804FDF7C32BD9A7FE9D417D14B3557F8D9F27B1DCCD34E4542D6D1FFF3","cid":"QmTjqBAAfPiGh76itTUCRmqpkN8drShhootsFRXa3FW8GL","occurredAt":"2026-10-07T06:15:37.509Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_0ac924499fc40cf8f4bc25524d6cec99","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_487a56091ee5f4fb6e5a4598ab5e0e6b","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Write and Merge Wallet-Linkage Onboarding Spec PR","description":"When a new contributor gets their first PF Terminal task, the system asks them to prove which wallet belongs to their account, but the request is confusing. The project site (postfiatorg.github.io, issue #5) records a real newcomer stuck on this: the task said to reply with 'the requested location and exact displayed address', but nothing in the app labels what a 'displayed address' is or where to find it. The goal of this task is to write one specification document that decides, once and for all, exactly how a first task should ask a newcomer to prove their wallet is linked to their account, so any newcomer can follow it without asking for help. The repo is github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal (open-source PF Terminal, current main branch head commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b). You will add ONE new file named FIRST-TASK-WALLET-LINKAGE-SPEC.md at the repository root (the repo already keeps spec documents at the root, so follow that same format) and open a pull request against the main branch. Do NOT change any program code. The spec must contain four things: (1) the decision to be made, stated plainly; (2) exact acceptance criteria for an unambiguous wallet-linkage request - what the newcomer is shown, exactly where in the terminal screen or profile it appears, and what counts as verified; (3) a concrete recommended resolution with your reasoning; (4) the validation steps someone would run to confirm the recommendation works. Any reference to a file, screen, or UI element must name the commit SHA where you verified it (for example, 'as of commit c9f358c0').","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_e16118dc90782249cd2d672a2ba4cafc","lastEvent":{"txHash":"09D7DE29D33D1EA74EF0D6A4965CA4087D5B982F5364376074BA98C17F04C43E","cid":"QmZBqv6XyBR4sFHFQBUDV3oudZz1UWDM88asyvBUXYwiMM","occurredAt":"2026-10-05T11:54:40.671Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_487a56091ee5f4fb6e5a4598ab5e0e6b","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_2d50eac96f98850e979abce86a1238c3","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce and Document the /resume TUI Freeze on CorbanuTerminal","description":"CorbanuTerminal is a terminal-based AI coding agent (GitHub repo: CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, written in Rust and TypeScript). Bug report issue #125 on that repo says that in version 0.1.44, typing the /resume command inside the app freezes the screen, even though opening an old session directly still works fine. There is an open fix, pull request #134, titled 'fix(tui): restore input in the active-session resume picker', which may or may not solve the freeze. Your job is not to write code. Your job is to test the bug yourself on both the normal code and the fix, write down exactly what happens in each case, and post your findings as a public comment on issue #125 so maintainers can confirm the bug and judge the fix. The finished work is one public, checkable comment on GitHub issue #125 containing the exact code version you tested, the commands you ran, what you saw before and after the fix, screenshots of the freeze, and your best guess at which files are involved.","rewardActualPft":0,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5fafefff458199c57b38eec6926722d5","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4FEDD940A4F710A8EBC8D69933611F70C7E60DC122B91F6F0C6101430B0DEDE6","cid":"QmYu8PKexY8bPAog4ABmvM5giBvGQVcisFFjVQU54AATeH","occurredAt":"2026-10-05T01:43:13.352Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_2d50eac96f98850e979abce86a1238c3","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_f4bec7ef5c4454dacbe0f7494ed35f16","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Find and Fix One Reproducible Bug in PostfiatL1V2","description":"The Post Fiat L1 codebase (the GitHub repository postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2, the node software for the Post Fiat blockchain) has open bug-hunting work. Your job: find one real, reproducible bug in the RPC layer, consensus, storage, or the Orchard/Halo2 zero-knowledge proof code, and fix it. You must first prove the bug exists with a concrete reproduction (the exact input you used, what wrong behavior you saw, and what should have happened instead), then write the smallest correct fix you can. The finished work is a pull request merged into the repository's main branch (currently at commit b9e7fb42) that includes the reproduction, a one-paragraph explanation of the root cause, and a new regression test that fails on the old code and passes with your fix. The existing test suite must still pass. Note: a similar Orchard fix was already done in the separate repository postfiatorg/postfiatd, so pick something new in postfiatl1v2 rather than redoing that work.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_e8fa302175765f208228fd76d9918083","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B87AA3A18054E8EF53C182645A0C5A3CE991459C1E5CF3220367B480171434AD","cid":"QmQ3Zbnzk1RrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T09:46:17.969Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_f4bec7ef5c4454dacbe0f7494ed35f16","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_47595378df40b59055656c27a885e155","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Test Bug-Fix Pull Requests #134 and #135 in CorbanuTerminal","description":"Two open pull requests in the Corbanu Terminal project each claim to fix a reported bug, and nobody has independently checked whether they actually work. Your job is to test both PRs on your own machine and post a PASS or FAIL review comment on each one — not to write fixes, merge anything, or change the repository.\n\nCorbanuTerminal is a terminal program (built with Rust and TypeScript) whose code lives at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. The two claims to check:\n\n- PR #134, 'fix(tui): restore input in the active-session resume picker,' claims to fix bug report #125: typing /resume inside the running app freezes the interface, while running `corbanu resume --last --all` from a normal command line works fine.\n- PR #135, 'fix(models): make Grok 4.7 explicit-choice until tier pricing is supported,' claims to fix bug report #127: the app automatically picks the Grok 4.7 model (an AI model it can use), and the cost it shows for long prompts is too low; the change makes Grok 4.7 a model you must choose yourself.\n\nDone means: for each PR you have built the PR's code, run the steps that trigger the bug on both the main branch (the repository's main line of code) and the PR build, and posted a step-by-step review comment on that PR ending with a clear PASS (the PR fixes the named bug) or FAIL (it does not). Anyone reading your comment should be able to repeat your test on their own machine and see the same result.\n\nPost the comments from the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account. Do not merge either PR and do not modify the repository. This task pays for the four li","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d4a288ecc2f1b0dc4493459beb35f3ac","lastEvent":{"txHash":"A7F642999D76425AC9E4B51E01F245EC5770063B92B245899E914B088A4123EF","cid":"QmZ3KvsNZZZfT8VBspT9EZaBGxayP41ivHE9mCJZ45eaz1","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T01:01:55.112Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_47595378df40b59055656c27a885e155","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_33d5bfc3e127eec46bc6c7d01674c5d4","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Review PR #124 Cache Marker Fix and Publish Verdict Gist","description":"A pull request (#124) in the CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal project claims to fix a cost bug in how AI chat-cache markers are placed. When a chat includes tool calls (assistant messages that trigger tools, followed by tool results), the cache markers — special flags that tell AI providers like Anthropic which conversation chunks to reuse cheaply — were staying stuck on the oldest messages instead of moving to the newest turn. This meant every new turn re-billed the entire growing conversation at full price. The PR says it changes only two files: codex-rs/core/src/client.rs (the main client code that builds chat requests) and codex-rs/core/src/client_tests.rs (its tests). The PR's head commit is 91639061bb37b81c41e0de45da1209aa44db9c8d. A separate task already investigated why the PR's automated checks are failing — those failures are known problems on the main branch (a duplicated label in a build file and a broken package download), not caused by this PR. Do not investigate the CI failures; focus on reviewing the code itself. Your finished work is a public GitHub gist that quotes the actual diff, checks each claim against the code, and gives a clear verdict.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_55deae841102fec85b24fb94dec97095","lastEvent":{"txHash":"81DEF0A9E37AB84A82DB0B1235BD5C81F9AB3D8ABF6CDDAC8A581705E8CA9DF8","cid":"QmcpnVmnoEwvBg32NjHws4SwpMFxZnA7tWUji4jRrnbHLR","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T01:01:31.137Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_33d5bfc3e127eec46bc6c7d01674c5d4","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_e3342bba2ac33629324ef378cbc6af45","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Fresh Merge-Verdict Gist for PR #103 insta Bump","description":"Decide whether a dependency-update pull request is safe to merge, and publish that decision as a public gist. The pull request is #103 in the GitHub repo CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal): an automated Dependabot update that bumps the Rust crate insta from version 1.46.3 to 1.48.0 in the /codex-rs folder, changing two lock files (codex-rs/Cargo.lock and MODULE.bazel.lock). insta is a snapshot-testing crate — it stores what test output should look like and fails a test when the real output no longer matches, so a version bump can change snapshot formats or assertion behavior. The pull request's automated checks (CI) currently show 16 failing and 31 passing. Someone published a merge verdict for this same pull request earlier, but at an older commit — that verdict is now out of date, so do not reuse or copy it. The pull request has since been updated; its latest commit (the head) is now 07642f8715308d4b3f04fbe9e59679c8f087c7f5, and that is the version you must analyze from scratch. The finished gist must list all 16 failing checks with links to each failing job, quote the exact failing log line for each one, classify each failure as pre-existing on main (meaning it fails on the main branch too, so the bump did not cause it) or potentially caused by the bump, check whether the base commit (the commit the pull request branched from) fails the identical set of checks, and end with a clear merge-or-fix recommendation plus next steps. This is read-only work: do not open, comment on, or modify any pull request.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9950538901d3f0fd328867c26a6e8249","lastEvent":{"txHash":"10E0610CAA826E87C6E5E906EDE4BAFB036E9871036280A61CF72F58C9A22883","cid":"QmbDcGVmozo4PNktVstP3KjaUibfeFZm6ospb2jDoxSjUn","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T01:01:18.814Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_e3342bba2ac33629324ef378cbc6af45","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_cdbe84a63b0414f50842c5ff3317f632","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Merge-Verdict Gist For CorbanuTerminal PR #130","description":"Goal: check whether pull request #130 in the CorbanuTerminal GitHub repository is safe to merge, and publish your answer as a public gist.\n\nCorbanuTerminal is our Rust terminal app; its code lives at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Pull request #130, titled \"fix(core): name nine literal arguments in PR126 tests\", adds small comments that label each argument at four call sites in the tests - for example /* count: */ in front of a number. These labels are needed because an automated GitHub check named \"Argument comment lint\" failed on an earlier pull request (#126) when test arguments were passed without names. That same check still fails on the current main branch, at commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b (the 40-character ID of the commit the main branch is on right now).\n\nYou will verify the pull request without merging it and without changing any code. You read the diff, quote the check's logs, spot-check the comments, and publish one verdict - MERGE or DO-NOT-MERGE - tied to the pull request's exact newest commit (called its \"head SHA\"). The finished work is a dated public gist that anyone can open, read, and re-run.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_7e9e83b1d8a6275a17a73222e636b4b3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"2709D74EFA797E8A2CF5A82DD987CC17332CB7C09D320666725B8D658A088DEC","cid":"QmNaiEbXc5As9VMnnvmYogVXJcnqEQwixL5jN5BbEhpY7d","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T01:00:51.646Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_cdbe84a63b0414f50842c5ff3317f632","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8d2300863a71871153cebdccc69aa1bf","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify PR #131 Zlib Pin Fix and Publish Verdict Gist","description":"CorbanuTerminal is an app whose code lives on GitHub at CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. It builds with Bazel, a build tool that downloads exact copies of libraries and checks each file against a saved file-name-plus-SHA-256 entry called a 'pin'. The pin for the zlib compression library used by its Rust build rules (a ruleset named rules_rs) on Ubuntu 24.04 'Noble' 64-bit Intel/AMD ('amd64') machines has gone stale, so a Bazel download step fails with a checksum mismatch. Pull request #131 ('fix(bazel): refresh rules_rs Noble amd64 zlib pin') updates that file name and checksum. Your job is to independently check that fix and publish a public GitHub gist with a one-word verdict — MERGE or DO-NOT-MERGE — tied to the pull request's exact newest commit, so the maintainers can decide whether to merge it. You will not merge anything or push any code; you only verify and publish. Heads-up: some checks in this repo fail on every pull request for unrelated reasons (a banned dependency and runner billing problems), so judge this fix by the zlib download step itself, not by overall check colors.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_4b90d353271dc5d4cbd10ae037256ed5","lastEvent":{"txHash":"1F4A9F0EBB160E5A83800B87E6DA84A442521B1A4A2B4225C587CBDBFDEC53CA","cid":"QmQD8A9hNPdNBMoW7cLs3jMtd11s2xP3SZS9GpAMbYHdTq","occurredAt":"2026-10-04T01:00:05.816Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8d2300863a71871153cebdccc69aa1bf","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_3e1d47d288fbbc17698295735bbc2ded","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Real Post Fiat Contribution With Checkable Proof","description":"Post Fiat paid this account 120,000 PFT across 6 past network tasks (commentary and audit write-ups), and a check is now running on whether that spending produced anything real for the network. You do not need to defend those past tasks — they were assigned by the system, not requested by you. Instead, show one real contribution you have made to Post Fiat from any work at all, assigned or not, with a link a reviewer can open and check. Honest answers are fine: if your assigned tasks did not add value, say so and point to what did. Only no response, or no checkable proof of any contribution at all, affects your future access to network tasks and rewards.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5f419d37e92b9e2faabea25fcb887a94","lastEvent":{"txHash":"F4292FA72597541BF17E4CF954570044FCC22D2489D89522E81E58EDA7822BA6","cid":"QmYeb2fCzn23aPtzNVhD5WX4NY3RJVAjyWQNBo44FdQRwp","occurredAt":"2026-10-03T18:50:17.087Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_3e1d47d288fbbc17698295735bbc2ded","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_0df62566d915ecc0cff4c87a99ce8ee6","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Real Post Fiat Contribution With Checkable Proof","description":"This is a one-time value check for your account. Background: Task Node previously assigned you three tasks that paid 300 PFT for writing commentary and review write-ups — a kind of work the network no longer pays for. Those tasks were chosen by Task Node, not by you, and you do not need to defend them or prove they had value. What this task asks instead: point to any real contribution you have made to Post Fiat, from any work at all — assigned or unassigned. For example: a merged pull request, a public gist that documented a bug or fix (you have several, such as your merged PR #48 smoke-test fix in the postfiatl1v2 repo and your public bug-verification gists), a post or thread on X about Post Fiat, a Discord message where you helped another member, or any user, partner, integration, or event you brought in. An honest answer is completely fine: if some of your assigned tasks did not add value, say so plainly and point to the work that did. Only two things fail this check: not responding at all, or providing no checkable proof of any contribution. Submit before 2026-10-04T02:57:43.831Z.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_ef3542342aa14e4d216c4c671122e084","lastEvent":{"txHash":"D2CD6DFC6FA90142E40E3646B5B5381D9061CE3FAEFCC9DE08D4AB619156FF8B","cid":"QmbF7qVgjvAeKdQCWrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-10-02T16:54:00.203Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_0df62566d915ecc0cff4c87a99ce8ee6","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_9fb3cc2da3e02e0bd9fe10a2f505af12","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Add Missing Devnet Storage Flag to Node Helper Scripts","description":"The node helper scripts in the Post Fiat L1 v2 repository (postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2 on GitHub) are missing a devnet storage flag, so anyone who uses those scripts to start a devnet node (devnet is the test network) either gets a failed startup or a node pointed at the wrong storage location. The finished work is a merged pull request on the repository's default branch (main) that adds the smallest correct fix and proves it works. Payment rule: this task pays only for a pull request you author with the GitHub account linked to your Task Node account and that is MERGED into main after this task was created. An open, unmerged, closed, or draft pull request will not be paid, and a pull request that already paid another task will not be paid again.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_60e55c62f64e8b7104b6b56a1b37c246","lastEvent":{"txHash":"54E6F247D7E1E1264194C792EC39D1433EA5C3D1793D99527D2F1633C22B0A62","cid":"QmWwo4ZSMueE9vdX9CbcJcDhvVkGna55MPcQ2itSVXY88e","occurredAt":"2026-10-01T14:39:29.827Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_9fb3cc2da3e02e0bd9fe10a2f505af12","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_5f92e0b56740a505691872454757566c","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Checkable Proof of Your Post Fiat Contribution","description":"This is a short check-in, not a defense of past work. Post Fiat's Task Node assigned your account 11 tasks in the past (paid 17,400 PFT) that were mostly write-ups commenting on published writing. The system chose those tasks, not you, so you do not have to prove they were worth the money. What this task asks instead: point to any real thing you have done that helped Post Fiat, from any work at all, assigned or not. To pass, you submit three things: (1) your Discord handle, (2) a link a reviewer can open that shows a contribution, and (3) one or two sentences explaining how it helped. Acceptable links include an X post or thread about Post Fiat, a Discord message where you helped a member, a merged pull request, a tool or integration you built, people or partners you brought in, or a community event you ran. Honesty is fine: if you think recent assigned tasks did not add value, say so and point to something that did. A quick confirming message from another Discord member is welcome but not required. Not responding at all, or responding with nothing a reviewer can open, is the only way to lose access to network tasks and rewards.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5ab389ac81babbd7ed038babd9a2c130","lastEvent":{"txHash":"D0E3F7BE9A8ED63E325A02A48D2581A00F91DBBF22408B87C5AFAF0FE64C25F9","cid":"QmPe6VzJe8uQEPKGeWybNXeYk7FoVvBB4W7iZzPYvskv3g","occurredAt":"2026-09-30T05:04:55.456Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_5f92e0b56740a505691872454757566c","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_728587f9b188c9322871e422c2da335a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Checkable Post Fiat Contribution You Made","description":"Post Fiat paid you 100 PFT for past tasks (published commentary and review write-ups) — work of a kind Post Fiat no longer pays for. You do not need to defend those tasks. Instead, this short check asks you to show one real contribution you have made to Post Fiat from any work at all, assigned or not, with a link a reviewer can open. If your recent assigned tasks did not add value, an honest answer is fine: say so and point to something that did. Submitting an honest response with at least one checkable link keeps your access to network tasks and rewards. Only no response, or no checkable proof of any contribution at all, removes that access.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_10ce70c54ce1169ae066bb53d27bddea","lastEvent":{"txHash":"7B9DD7E3665865A557AF33B8C09815233604538AC1782B81FB5781BFE090D2A0","cid":"QmZUuikVXvMJwzjPJUYc9b77kg89NhmqemmrJgd1AxnNJt","occurredAt":"2026-09-29T06:18:37.396Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_728587f9b188c9322871e422c2da335a","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_69ec186d8d27e6c38aecfaa12a9476ee","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Submit Value Check With Discord Handle and Contribution Link","description":"Goal: reply to a one-time check from the network by showing, with a link anyone can open, one real contribution you have made to Post Fiat. This is not a test of your past assigned tasks — the system, not you, chose those, and you do not need to defend them. You only need to point to something real you did that helped Post Fiat's value or adoption, from any work at all (assigned tasks, your own projects, helping people in Discord, posts on X about Post Fiat, code you merged, people or partners you brought in, community events — anything that can be checked by opening a link). An honest answer is welcome: if you think your recent assigned tasks did not add value, say so and point to what did. Only staying silent, or giving no checkable proof of any contribution, changes your access to network tasks and rewards.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f1795f32b2c9125f8faf5d978cfd8e98","lastEvent":{"txHash":"36839DE144E0A0032442A38A3F3D4D1408E395FBEFADB80ADC0D851E1A0C99F4","cid":"QmRuysZhQLN25rREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-09-29T02:56:12.263Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_69ec186d8d27e6c38aecfaa12a9476ee","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_18fa35efba33263dc71fdd23202e55cd","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Real Post Fiat Contribution With Proof","description":"This is a value check, not a work assignment. Task Node paid you 22,750 PFT across three tasks that were commentary or review write-ups — the kind of work the network no longer pays for. You were assigned those tasks by Task Node, so you don't need to defend them or prove they added value. Instead, show any real contribution you have made to Post Fiat from any work at all, assigned or not. The finished submission is short: your Discord handle, one link a reviewer can actually open that shows something you did that helped Post Fiat's value or adoption, and one or two sentences explaining how it helped. Honest answers are fine — if your recent assigned tasks didn't add value, say so and point to what did. Only a non-response, or no checkable proof of any contribution at all, removes access to network tasks and rewards.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_13708cbc26214ffe5e9daeac87a79c55","lastEvent":{"txHash":"401BFD1793A8C489582EF163E585991A1F306A5E54D9089B8AD8955B7A4D7685","cid":"Qmf5rREDACTEDrqJKCLY","occurredAt":"2026-09-28T22:03:49.819Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_18fa35efba33263dc71fdd23202e55cd","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_0c6be6d74badb0441e9aae6a077e82cd","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Checkable Post Fiat Contribution With Proof","description":"The Post Fiat network paid you 13,905 PFT across 14 past tasks (mostly commentary and audit write-ups), and the network chose those tasks — you do not need to defend them. What is needed now is one simple check that you have made any real contribution to Post Fiat, from any work at all, assigned or not. Submit three things: your Discord handle, a link a reviewer can open that shows something you did that helped Post Fiat (for example: an X post or thread about Post Fiat, a Discord message where you helped a member, a merged pull request, a bug report, users or partners you brought in, a community event), and one or two sentences on how it helped. An honest answer is fine — if some of your past work did not add value, say so and point to what did. Only no response at all, or no checkable proof of any contribution, removes access to network tasks and rewards.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_ac9755622974648cf439481ac60f54f1","lastEvent":{"txHash":"57841CFEF1AC75D6AC4E3ABFF02E7AA292B85484BBCD49C251E7C1BC0C54CD1B","cid":"QmexP7WMjfqEQivxbVUNgJ5MdwyzjLrHsQ4eAupWA48h8a","occurredAt":"2026-09-28T15:42:37.803Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_0c6be6d74badb0441e9aae6a077e82cd","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a6689a2f23e189f1905b7af8414e90c0","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Real Contribution to Post Fiat","description":"Post Fiat paid you 113,950 PFT across 10 tasks for commentary and audit write-ups — work that Task Node no longer pays for. Task Node chose those tasks, not you, so you do not need to defend them or prove they added value. Instead, point to any single real contribution you have made to Post Fiat, from any work at all, whether it was an assigned task or not. An honest answer is fine: if your recent assigned tasks did not add value, say so and point to what did. This is a simpler version of a prior task (task_4c5f, titled 'Prove Your Ten Paid Tasks Added Market Value') that was refused because it required proving cause-and-effect for all ten paid tasks. This version only asks for one checkable link and a short explanation.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_ecd40ca9bc125a3a7ce5b5eadc6cdec1","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B2CA56BA0E625E940103A7733408B08C8F978FF8DB20E8A53F44AD89C614C141","cid":"QmWpNLT2k87t1MG2KSMtu4XEP76MXv6CYTg4aWjvnWHEJ2","occurredAt":"2026-09-28T14:50:12.178Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a6689a2f23e189f1905b7af8414e90c0","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_bb43bbd9b78383a521f7423c6e487c19","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Submit One Checkable Link Showing a Real Post Fiat Contribution","description":"Goal: show one real thing you did that helped Post Fiat, with a link a reviewer can open. Background: Task Node paid this account 84,700 PFT across 14 past tasks of a kind that is no longer paid for (commentary and audit write-ups). Task Node chose those tasks, so you do not need to defend them or prove they created results. This is not that. This task simply asks you to point to any genuine contribution you have made to Post Fiat, from any work at all, assigned or not. An honest answer is welcome: if you think some past assigned tasks added no value, you can say so and point to what did. Only a missing reply, or a reply with no checkable proof of any contribution, affects access to future network tasks.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_1cd04df8413395ab9a06f63d2f1957d0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9B2D1EA8E64818CABB3722FF7F2AC5641B58F293C00219AA5F90618FADD8563B","cid":"QmXQQXBkcfnJiZhCsqXnz8RSHR3scUuRyr9bSHYHpQy441","occurredAt":"2026-09-28T14:11:09.454Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_bb43bbd9b78383a521f7423c6e487c19","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_6bfcc70557dc34f9193126f3ee2e7145","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Show One Checkable Post Fiat Contribution For Value Review","description":"Post Fiat paid this account 200 PFT total for two past network tasks (commentary on published writing, and audit or review write-ups) - task types the system no longer pays for. You were assigned those tasks by the system, so you do not need to defend them or prove they added value. Instead, this task asks you to show any real contribution you have made to Post Fiat, from any work at all, assigned or not. The finished submission is simple: your Discord handle, at least one link a reviewer can open that shows a contribution to Post Fiat's value or adoption (for example, an X post or thread about Post Fiat, a Discord message where you helped a member or brought someone in, a merged pull request, an integration, users, partners, or liquidity you brought, a community event, or anything else that can be checked), and one or two sentences on how it helped. An honest answer is fine: if your recent assigned tasks did not add value, say so and point to what did. Only submitting nothing, or submitting no checkable proof of any contribution at all, removes access to network tasks and rewards. A confirming message from another Discord member is welcome but optional.","rewardActualPft":1,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_ac6e47ffc4588419566462d5ac972cd0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"321C1A806C5340DD06BF13F1CE029B887D9F8E342BEF5559E55777A050BA99CA","cid":"QmT8qvjhvAGoPeL8dGBXKzHsiB2kVq14XBktZ9B2QYqH9d","occurredAt":"2026-09-28T12:56:54.438Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_6bfcc70557dc34f9193126f3ee2e7145","project":{"id":"board_value_accountability","title":"Value Accountability","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_7557b2025ed57455d28b58ea175a2806","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish a Medium Critique of 'The Nigeria Template'","description":"Write and publish a public Medium article that critiques the essay 'The Nigeria Template' by goodalexander (a Post Fiat community member). The essay is a long-form piece about Nigeria's economic and political situation; you can read it at https://goodalexander.github.io/posts/the-nigeria-template/ (the source text lives in the goodalexander/goodalexander.github.io GitHub repository under content/posts/the-nigeria-template.md, if you prefer reading the raw Markdown). The goal: give readers a fair, evidence-based assessment of whether the essay's big claims hold up. The finished work is a published Medium article anyone can open by URL.","rewardActualPft":1000,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_0aee315d5138d724302d2432c7d37bea","lastEvent":{"txHash":"B7E2DCE33EA0EE143D0C04856ECBBA77AC75C5FD7D4BEE75BF7E1464B43F8F2A","cid":"Qmayk9iSKSQbdVND7vVtk2wckY1LxkhagpF8K3TaAHQhUC","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T20:46:52.662Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_7557b2025ed57455d28b58ea175a2806","project":{"id":"board_capital_markets","title":"Capital Markets","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_b37990d465f5bacebbccfb6915b70bd1","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Reproduce Issue 28 Monitor Smoke on Clean Main","description":"Bug report #28 in the postfiatl1v2 GitHub repo says a test called testnet-monitor-snapshot-smoke always fails on a brand-new machine that runs only transparent (non-private) transactions: the test warns 'proof_latency_unavailable' even though nothing is actually broken. Two pull requests tried to fix this: PR #46 (a first warning fix) and PR #48 (a second fix that made the test pass on fresh machines). Both may now be merged into the main branch. Your job: check out a fresh copy of the repo at today's main commit, confirm whether the fix code from PR #48 is actually present, then run the smoke test path exactly as a fresh machine would and record whether it passes or fails. Finish by publishing your results as a public GitHub gist with the exact commands you ran, the commit hash you tested, and the pass/fail output, and paste the gist link as your submission.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d6cd5a75e5253a7acad385b0a2a56444","lastEvent":{"txHash":"9DDAACDFB5B774BDE58E12D65989BE24A6EED39B664B5E65BFCAAC209F0DA758","cid":"QmaKt1duLw5cnAxnPZpeGSroz5cF64eiZmcJ1P2Gfnip3S","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T19:42:40.747Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_b37990d465f5bacebbccfb6915b70bd1","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_3afbd480c9449ad8c3960947408784de","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Merge-Verdict Gist for PR #102 opentelemetry_sdk Bump","description":"Decide whether pull request #102 in the CorbanuTerminal repository (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) is safe to merge, and publish your verdict as a public gist so the maintainers know whether to merge it or fix something first. PR #102 is an automated dependency-update pull request from Dependabot titled 'Bump opentelemetry_sdk from 0.31.0 to 0.32.1 in /codex-rs'; it changes one line in codex-rs/Cargo.toml plus the Cargo.lock file, and its head commit is d92b955f1bc4d0f97d5974b34fb4c7c6ebf4fcdb. The pull request's automated test runs (CI) currently show 22 failing checks, including Windows Bazel shards, musl release builds, cargo shear, and cargo-deny. A 0.31-to-0.32 bump looks 'minor', but this crate can still change its code interfaces in minor releases and break builds, so do not assume the failures are unrelated — open each failing job's log and classify every failure yourself as either already broken before the bump or possibly caused by it. The finished work is one public gist listing all 22 failing checks with job URLs, quoting the exact failing log line for each, comparing against the CI of the commit the pull request is based on, and ending with a clear merge verdict plus required follow-up steps. This is read-only work: do not comment on, reopen, or modify any pull request, and do not change repository code.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_d5167e23d916b18e3f478dfd048958df","lastEvent":{"txHash":"F701A1FBD131591A245998C5F51E2DB43A323B1A09690469953C7AE406AA023D","cid":"QmdoCE6ZpjDm5kC14gL7Ci7S4D7EwwfAHa7M7awcKQhgL1","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T18:44:36.772Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_3afbd480c9449ad8c3960947408784de","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_b5cd9b04e62abaf4577b8b5ddf839ef7","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Retrospective Claim Audit Gist of New Beginnings Essay","description":"In one sentence: a 2021 markets essay made specific, checkable predictions, and your job is to quote each prediction word-for-word, check it against dated public records, and publish the results as a public GitHub gist with a claim-by-claim scorecard.\n\nBackground: In January 2021, a markets writer known as goodalexander published an essay titled 'New Beginnings' on his personal blog - a free website hosted on GitHub (repository goodalexander/goodalexander.github.io, file content/posts/new-beginnings.md, dated 2021-01-02). The essay made dated, checkable predictions, including: Bitcoin would go parabolic; a VanEck Bitcoin ETF (a fund that would let regular stock-market investors buy Bitcoin price exposure) was coming soon; 10-year breakeven inflation (a bond-market gauge of expected inflation) would sit near 2% while the Federal Reserve let the economy 'run hot'; the Chapwood Index (an unofficial cost-of-living tracker) showed real inflation of 10-11% in major U.S. cities; and a Democratic 'Blue Wave' was increasingly likely in Georgia's January 5, 2021 Senate runoff.\n\nContext: The Capital Markets board (the Post Fiat project that assigns and rewards this research) has already published fact-check gists of other essays by the same author. This task covers only 'New Beginnings' - do not re-audit essays already covered.\n\nThe finished gist must contain exactly five sections:\n1. The essay's URL plus the commit hash (GitHub's ID for a saved version of a file) of the exact copy you read, so anyone can confirm which text you audited.\n2. Every dated prediction, quoted word-for-word.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_2cd98b0f175579ecf5a064bde39d6780","lastEvent":{"txHash":"EE92053EE9442029B2606563D226D8212056F29AE078421333CB0A254A80D183","cid":"QmRpKDQvvdvXiBiYz3piu6qDEEV3YFppMsatFFf3DQNTDQ","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T16:03:23.805Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_b5cd9b04e62abaf4577b8b5ddf839ef7","project":{"id":"board_capital_markets","title":"Capital Markets","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_2d93f8c815f61f7402543fa67d353c06","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify Issue #128 Missing Output Token Limits and Publish Gist","description":"Someone reported a bug (issue #128) in the CorbanuTerminal app's model catalog, which is the built-in list of AI models the app can call. The report says six retired (older, mostly unused) model rows are missing a value called max_output_tokens, which caps how long an AI model's reply can be. The six rows are: x-ai/grok-4.6, openrouter/owl-alpha, x-ai/grok-4.5, deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro, deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731, and gpt-5.5. The report claims these six rows are missing the cap in two versions of the code: the base commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b (an older snapshot of the code) and the head commit 64ffe30dd94f986bf5a9e7ccc5e9f25c958d4c39 (the version the report was written against). It also claims each of the six rows is hidden from users and turned off for automatic model selection, while a comparison row, deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813, still has the cap set to 384000, and all seven newly added rows have positive caps. This task is read-only: do not change any code, open any pull request, or push anything. Your finished work is a public gist (a shareable web page at gist.github.com) showing the exact command outputs, your yes/no verdict for each claim, and an analysis of what actually happens when a user picks one of these models by name. Note: this is a different issue from #129 (stale token and context values), which was already checked and rewarded — do not repeat that work.","rewardActualPft":125,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9b1bd72f8fdda6bdfb1a8ef1efe83f4c","lastEvent":{"txHash":"276FA9246BB61CB3D0515AB87D364697804D361D69D4749B71A3F36A588B3FD5","cid":"QmaRUqj9ECi4UK3FnTrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T15:37:10.725Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_2d93f8c815f61f7402543fa67d353c06","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_b92e97ffc5be85ebafa03dfd849914d6","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Public Critique Gist of Enlightened Hedonism Essay","description":"Goal: read one public essay, check whether its main claim holds up against public evidence, and publish your findings as a public critique page on GitHub.\n\nThe essay is 'Enlightened Hedonism' by a writer named goodalexander. His blog is a public GitHub repository called goodalexander/goodalexander.github.io, and the essay lives in the file content/posts/enlightened-hedonism.md on its master branch. The last known change to that file is commit da9c72a85c1f194145ef708c5e06663c9e658f7e, dated 2023-12-29 — a commit is a saved snapshot of a repository, and the hash is that snapshot's ID. Before starting, you must confirm yourself which commit currently touches the file, because the hash you cite proves you read today's text and not an old copy.\n\nThe finished deliverable is one public GitHub gist (a gist is a free public text page anyone can open, created at gist.github.com with any GitHub account) with six fixed sections: the essay URL plus the commit hash of the exact copy you read; a short summary of the argument in your own words; the essay's central claim copied word for word; an evidence check naming at least 3 public sources with a one-line verdict each (at least one source must undercut or complicate the claim); a rewrite of the central claim into a form that could be proven wrong with evidence; and a list of essay claims that public sources cannot check. Use only public sources — nothing behind a login or paywall, no credentials, no private material. When the gist is live, announce it in an approved Post Fiat Discord channel and submit the gist URL, its revision id, the ","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_507a76b237a346d1b0358f4709b64a35","lastEvent":{"txHash":"7C8E1DD4128AD3E9BA55439D49CD4050A9EAB0F484C25466810D52AE3807A63B","cid":"QmXEvL6SFDLaZoVhugSTR6Jkuej9ZK9aHMAuiwGusHdYgr","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T15:32:00.019Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_b92e97ffc5be85ebafa03dfd849914d6","project":{"id":"board_capital_markets","title":"Capital Markets","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_ed6783362565302df0888f99d3e7aaa7","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Resume Picker Typing Bug And Open PR","description":"Goal: in the CorbanuTerminal terminal app (GitHub repository CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal), the /resume picker ignores everything you type — you open it to search your past chat sessions, and your keystrokes never appear in the search box. Fix this with one small code change and open a pull request (PR — a proposed change on GitHub that maintainers can review).\n\nThe cause is already diagnosed and was paid for, so do not repeat the investigation. The public bug report is GitHub issue #125 in that repository. The full diagnosis — including a reproduce.py script and a recorded .cast replay of the bug — is here: https://gist.github.com/JJ2203-theRealOne/4f4a8756b9c43758e122b61f8a70682f\n\nWhat is broken: the picker is built by a function called run_session_picker_with_loader in the file codex-rs/tui/src/resume_picker.rs (around lines 460-475). When the picker opens, it creates its own brand-new stream of keyboard events. But the main app already runs a background loop that reads and throws away those same events, so your keys never reach the picker — two readers share one keyboard and the picker loses.\n\nThe fix (keep it as small as possible — only the lines needed): in codex-rs/tui/src/app/event_dispatch.rs (around line 864), the app reacts to an event called AppEvent::OpenResumePicker when the picker opens. Make that event's handler borrow the app's existing keyboard receiver — the field tui_event_rx, the queue the app already uses to receive key presses — and pass it into run_session_picker_with_loader instead of letting the picker create a fresh event_stream(). A nearby handler","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_9b3a33aaeebdcd35e16b4b9a87a3e54b","lastEvent":{"txHash":"069EB68C90EBA1961A59D766D0245EAD096B61548C74D03AA0E1471B2ED1421B","cid":"QmcE8qnbxXAmHL4QxbUanUEnE5sT7udYEMkWzxrYcf2EhJ","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T15:10:28.668Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_ed6783362565302df0888f99d3e7aaa7","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_d15db0497d6630805a9cd16e7ead4632","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Expert Critique Gist of Retrofixation Essay","description":"Goal: write a rigorous four-part critique of the essay 'Retrofixation' by the writer goodalexander, publish it as a public gist, and announce it in the Post Fiat Discord. 'Retrofixation' is a 2023 essay (about 13,000 characters) that coins a term for treating the past as a fixed anchor and argues this harms investing, decisions, and mood. It is free to read at https://goodalexander.com/posts/retrofixation/ . Your critique must have four parts: (1) pull out the essay's main claims from each of its three sections (money, emotions, society), quoting the essay word-for-word wherever you make a point about it; (2) give each claim its strongest version, then test it: where a claim can be checked against real-world data, cite at least one dated, linked source (for example, behavioral-finance research on recency bias or anchoring, or documented cases where studying history beat gut-feel investing); where a claim is just an opinion that cannot be tested as written, say so plainly and propose a version that could be tested; (3) check the essay against itself: it warns against living in the past, yet uses past stories (Steve Jobs's Apple, investor Stanley Druckenmiller) as its own evidence — is that a contradiction or not?; (4) end with a verdict on which parts hold up and which do not. Analysis only: no investment advice or trade recommendations. Keep secrets out of everything you publish.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5d429219779adf7255acbb7f0d10e367","lastEvent":{"txHash":"02826CF56F5B4D8FD70E8C873E8BC8878974C47688D987244ED7186CC35ECB1D","cid":"QmZj53yQD4ccZ46QjpdBQvcBdSpQCMeAHNqkQvT3KaUEZo","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T14:54:00.764Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_d15db0497d6630805a9cd16e7ead4632","project":{"id":"board_capital_markets","title":"Capital Markets","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_a7af02bb0ec3d7aa5d8cdfca17cb1e13","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Verify Issue #127 Grok 4.7 Pricing Claims in a Public Gist","description":"A bug report (issue #127) in the CorbanuTerminal repository claims that the app's cost estimates for the x-ai/grok-4.7 model are too low for very long prompts. The report says the app's model catalogue lists flat prices of $1.60 per million input tokens, $4.80 per million output tokens, and $0.40 per million cache tokens, but OpenRouter (the service that actually routes these requests) charges double those rates once a prompt reaches 200,000 tokens. The app's billing data structure may have no way to express this second, higher price tier. The finished work is a public GitHub gist that quotes the exact lines of code and catalogue data at a specific commit, captures the live OpenRouter pricing feed with a timestamp, shows the dollar gap for a 250,000-token prompt, and gives a CONFIRMED, REFUTED, or PARTIALLY-CONFIRMED verdict for each claim. This is read-only verification: do not modify any code, open pull requests, or push anything to the repository.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_cd3a3f011d35e6a7a1cd972771b2e0e3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"0EEC6D1FC95968383519662A00ABF5515240D22FD7ABF3D5B2AE735A1D67CFE7","cid":"QmeuQQPHdfVDMng9xtXACha3gQnHPDioyLc9TqrPVRA7Rz","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T14:45:19.674Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_a7af02bb0ec3d7aa5d8cdfca17cb1e13","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_9ac5c42c356e2a46c4080ed7972c83f8","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Investigate Failing CI on Four Dependabot PRs, Publish Readiness Gist","description":"Four open pull requests in the GitHub repository CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal are dependency robots' updates to the CI workflow files (they only change which versions of GitHub helper tools the automated tests use, not the project's Rust code). All four show the same 18 failing automated checks, which suggests the failures come from a shared problem in the main branch or the test setup, not from these small version bumps — but nobody has checked that yet. Your job: read-only investigation of the real CI logs for each PR, figure out whether the red checks are actually caused by the PRs or by something else, and publish one public gist (on gist.github.com) that states a merge verdict for each PR so the maintainers can act on it. Do not open, edit, comment on, or push anything to the repository — this is read-only.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_e78e53cab7de0b443dd22eb5ca04c7f0","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4EFCF77D9238DC27D4314BBDD873146162D2DE003CC52864DDF3F60F7DC13244","cid":"QmaRPRXCBsZmVDSmjLNC6JFwTwFEbEKpxyjUhGgo1NTNca","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T14:38:02.735Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_9ac5c42c356e2a46c4080ed7972c83f8","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_129ce603c3c31dd92204b832f6598a31","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish reqwest 0.12 to 0.13 Migration-Readiness Gist for CorbanuTerminal","description":"CorbanuTerminal, a Rust terminal app (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal), currently builds with two copies of reqwest — a common Rust library programs use to make HTTP web requests: the old 0.12.28 and the new 0.13.4. Fourteen packages in the build still depend on the old 0.12.28 copy, and the maintainers want to finish the move to 0.13 one package at a time. Your job: find out, for each of those 14 packages, the exact reason it is still on 0.12.28 and whether it can be moved today or must wait for an outside library to update first, then publish the answer as a public gist that names the first pull request someone should open next.\n\nThe 14 packages are nine crates owned by the repo (codex-app-server, codex-browser-isolation, codex-cli, codex-gpu-market, codex-http-client, codex-otel, codex-responses-api-proxy, codex-tui, codex-wallet) and five outside libraries (oauth2, opentelemetry-http, opentelemetry-otlp, sentry, teloxide-core). Do all reading at the exact repository snapshot (commit) c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b, because reviewers will re-check every claim against codex-rs/Cargo.lock (the file recording the exact version of every library used), each crate's Cargo.toml (the file where a crate lists its dependencies), and codex-rs/deny.toml (the repo's dependency-rule file, which bans new direct reqwest use everywhere except codex-http-client, the crate meant to be the app's single HTTP wrapper). This is read-only analysis: do not modify the repository and do not open a pull request — the immediate follow-up action is the first migration pull request yo","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_777ed3ea678d39a0b871d5cf5c9cc3ed","lastEvent":{"txHash":"6BBEEBD5D47F341A3622CC853B6B7356C1FDF8A779E87CC85D9309AC9B02277A","cid":"QmYS1tsu9bthj9xeFf2w1MBYxxAXTJdRkCGcrhB4Hogix8","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T14:25:49.805Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_129ce603c3c31dd92204b832f6598a31","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_fc6df516aacec1cb610a100239dd7053","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Publish Critique Gist of Stepping into Phase Seven Essay","description":"Goal: read one specific published essay and post a public, fact-checked critique of its main claim. The essay is 'Stepping into Phase Seven' by goodalexander, who is also the operator behind the Capital Markets board, the project this task belongs to. It is a public file on GitHub: content/posts/entering-phase-seven.md in the repository goodalexander/goodalexander.github.io, on the master branch. The author splits market history into numbered phases, and this essay is about the one after 'Phase 6' — in particular, who becomes the trusted gatekeepers of financial information and why. Your job is to pin that central claim down in the author's own words, then check it against real public evidence. A gist is a single public web page on gist.github.com that anyone can open without logging in. The finished gist must have six parts: (1) the essay's web address plus the commit hash — the Git version ID of the exact copy you read, so a reviewer can confirm you critiqued what is actually published; (2) a short summary of the essay's argument in your own words; (3) the central claim copied word for word from the essay; (4) an evidence check naming at least 3 checkable public sources — for example, public reporting on the collapses of Three Arrows Capital, Archegos, or Melvin Capital (well-documented fund failures), or public data on whether popular individual finance creators actually replaced institutional financial media — with a one-line verdict for each source: supports the claim or undercuts it; (5) a falsifiability note — can the claim be tested? If not, rewrite it into a versio","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f05a227c3ce9487b9ce6b48b381b9b94","lastEvent":{"txHash":"852DF1CFD5A474C480CD77B2457A69BA979659A591AA06D13EDCCBE9D1D3EE8F","cid":"QmXQKGQKMNwGnR2pAuhZ8BxLxMgkonU4EPVjgGDQErka9W","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T11:49:53.873Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_fc6df516aacec1cb610a100239dd7053","project":{"id":"board_capital_markets","title":"Capital Markets","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_8a3b360ffd0f6ce04004ea1b72272e7a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Open PR Bumping rustls to 0.23.45 in CorbanuTerminal","description":"CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, a Rust terminal app) fails its dependency security check on main because codex-rs/Cargo.lock - the file that freezes the exact versions of every Rust package the app uses - still pins rustls 0.23.36. That version is covered by RUSTSEC-2026-0285, a published security report saying TLS 1.3 handshake messages were being accepted across encryption-level boundaries; the flaw is fixed in rustls 0.23.45 and later. The finished work is one small pull request that bumps rustls to 0.23.45, refreshes the related Bazel lock file, and shows the code still compiles.\n\nContext: cargo-deny (a tool that compares a project's locked package versions against published security reports) flags this on main commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b, and no open pull request fixes it yet. A read-only investigation of this exact problem was already completed and rewarded - the public note is at gist.github.com/citadelculture/7a82e9f9aea119e1eacf3eb5399678eb. It trial-ran the update command (computing the change without saving it) and proved that bumping rustls also moves exactly three companion packages: aws-lc-rs 1.16.2->1.18.1, aws-lc-sys 0.39.0->0.45.0, and rustls-webpki 0.103.13->0.103.15. This task is the follow-up: turn that proven fix into the real pull request. Do not redo the investigation.\n\nKeep the change minimal: only the lockfile updates named in the steps. Do not edit any Cargo.toml (those files state which versions are allowed; only the lock file, which records the exact versions in use, should change), do not bump any oth","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_5ac116b22917780be35d02bd1e240f78","lastEvent":{"txHash":"FFCDA2AC0EC0292235F86BC81408DF2556EECC533F04DE80B2227364E083DBA8","cid":"QmdVzFRPa9tpjnT6XSTmMdbAhvsEtmfmvYn76YWSt7Rcep","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T11:21:31.494Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_8a3b360ffd0f6ce04004ea1b72272e7a","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_d998ec772979690a6bb6b9ad844e39fd","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Investigate RUSTSEC-2026-0285 rustls Advisory In CorbanuTerminal cargo-deny","description":"A security check in the CorbanuTerminal project is failing because the build pulls in rustls 0.23.36, a library for secure network connections (TLS) that has a published security flaw; the finished work is a public gist that shows exactly how that flawed library gets into the build and the smallest change that would replace it with a fixed version. Background you need: CorbanuTerminal is a Rust terminal app; its code lives at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal. Its CI (the automatic checks that run on every change) includes cargo-deny, a tool that scans the project's package list for banned packages and known security flaws. On the current main branch (commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b), that check fails with an advisory against rustls 0.23.36: RUSTSEC-2026-0285, a real published flaw where rustls wrongly accepts certain TLS 1.3 handshake messages across encryption-level boundaries. (The same failing job also marks reqwest 0.12.28 as banned; that error is separate and out of scope for this task.) The failure was uncovered during earlier CI debugging on pull request #126, a bug-fix pull request on the same repo, and no task has covered this advisory yet. Two libraries bring rustls into the project: hyper-rustls v0.27.7 and rama-tls-rustls v0.3.0-alpha.4. This job is strictly read-only: do not open a pull request, do not change repository files, and do not push anything. Your gist goes to the PF Terminal project reviewer, who will use it to plan the actual fix, so it must stand alone with nothing missing.","rewardActualPft":125,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_f7c2cc58f603395c50689b7ac875eec3","lastEvent":{"txHash":"DB358D5797E3818EEEB3A2510095E1106AA30758B4A5E3E6EA2FE979ECB582D3","cid":"QmTR5UP1ATds7qQNxuQWrREDACTED","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T10:58:23.517Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_d998ec772979690a6bb6b9ad844e39fd","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_46ee37b3029fb037da66fc6834d80591","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Add Missing Cargo Build Step to tmux Smoke Workflow","description":"Goal: the CorbanuTerminal project's tmux test job on GitHub fails on every run because the script that runs it never builds the command-line programs the tests try to launch. Your job is to open a pull request that adds the one missing build line.\n\nBackground: In the repository github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal, the file .github/workflows/tmux-smoke.yml is a GitHub Actions workflow - a script GitHub's servers run automatically on pushes. It switches into the codex-rs folder and runs the tmux test suite, but no step in it ever builds the codex and corbanu command-line programs that the tests try to launch, so the job stops with the error 'Error: could not locate binary codex' / 'build corbanu first'. An earlier paid investigation traced this to the missing build step and wrote down the exact one-line fix; its notes are in the public gist a4951309. No open pull request applies the fix, and the defect is still present at the repository's current main commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b.\n\nFinished work looks like: one pull request against CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal whose diff adds exactly one build step to that workflow file and changes nothing else, plus the validation notes listed in the steps below.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_6cd9047511085d398dc90c2cab6bf653","lastEvent":{"txHash":"5167D66FE00D93244FBE4D7964C97B0B26EFA0F4BB5182377FC9472832A63266","cid":"QmQE2kGa2m9AV4gJ6KxNCLj947QNRDvVXNihYW5Cx2V54X","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T10:37:14.578Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_46ee37b3029fb037da66fc6834d80591","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_aa25c47a9b0ecf263602fe9aa9d51bdc","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Investigate Missing CLI Build In CorbanuTerminal tmux Smoke Workflow","description":"A required test job in CorbanuTerminal - the Rust terminal app at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal - fails on every run: it runs terminal tests without first compiling the command-line program ('binary') those tests try to launch. Your job is a read-only investigation: pin down exactly which build step is missing, and publish a public gist (a shareable text page at gist.github.com) that names the exact one-line fix, so a maintainer can repair the workflow by pasting one line.\n\nBackground: GitHub runs automatic checks from files in the repo's .github/workflows folder. The file .github/workflows/tmux-smoke.yml at main commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b (around lines 30-55) installs tmux (a tool that lets one terminal window hold several sessions) and nextest (a Rust test runner), then runs 'just test -p codex-tui --test all tmux --retries 0'. 'just' is a command runner that reads its instructions from a file named justfile. No step in this workflow builds the CLI binary first, so the job dies with: 'Error: Corbanu CLI binary with internal Claude-auth helpers is unavailable; build corbanu first' and 'Error: could not locate binary'. The failure was first flagged while reviewing pull request #126 (a proposed code change in this repo), but it happens on the main branch too, so that pull request is not the cause.\n\nThis is strictly read-only: do not open a pull request, edit any file, or push anything. Your gist is the deliverable; the maintainer's immediate next step after reading it is to add the one build line you identify.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_913431f72b7426d3c64270560aa35009","lastEvent":{"txHash":"97B5EBE623DF0707FAADA785AEA9DAF129D4C2071E12F34549591AF2B5E91C18","cid":"QmcWFKTJRKs54aCccYbcvoa8zqGCVnPM6uakytxnaWZfkk","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T10:05:41.512Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_aa25c47a9b0ecf263602fe9aa9d51bdc","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_6dadb12a9609e7c2df503879345a7e67","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Review Reserve-Proof Soundness in Pull Request 49","description":"The Post Fiat protocol repo (github.com/postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2) has an open pull request, PR #49, titled 'Bound NEAR record age and prove Aave debt completeness in the reserve proof' at head commit 670fa615. This PR changes the code that proves the protocol's reserves are backed correctly: it adds an age limit on NEAR blockchain records and a check that no Aave V3 debt position is silently missing. If the age limit is wrong or a debt position can be skipped without detection, the reserve proof could report money that is not really there. Nobody has reviewed this PR yet. Your finished work is a published, public review of the PR's code changes with a clear verdict, shared with the community.","rewardActualPft":125,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_2465e1ad3c749d5ee40a18915ea3fa2d","lastEvent":{"txHash":"194FCA98A4C84333EEE8A37D7C403B81939D0286E56C888889024CD78E91B9F7","cid":"QmSrREDACTEDbucHCdwF","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T09:48:00.670Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_6dadb12a9609e7c2df503879345a7e67","project":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","title":"PostfiatL1V2","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_4c54c19b2b303982032a572b2979f10d","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Bazel zlib 404 With Patch PR In CorbanuTerminal","description":"Goal: every Ubuntu build job in CorbanuTerminal fails before the code even compiles, because the build tries to download a zlib package that Ubuntu deleted from its servers. The finished work is one open pull request that points the build at the zlib package Ubuntu currently serves, plus proof that the download works again.\n\nWhat is broken: CorbanuTerminal (github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) builds with a tool called Bazel on Ubuntu machines. Its Rust build rules (rules_rs 0.0.102) hard-code this download: https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_amd64.deb. Ubuntu removed that file, so the download returns 404 (not found), and five CI jobs fail during setup: clippy (the code-style check), the GNU test, the musl test, verify-release, and the SDK job. An earlier investigation of this exact failure, published as public gist f97a518f, traced the cause and worked out the fix; this task writes that fix into the repo.\n\nHow the fix fits the repo: the repo's MODULE.bazel file (Bazel's dependency list, like a package manifest) already has a block at lines 93-101 that replaces rules_rs with a locally patched copy, applying patch files from the patches/ folder. One patch (rules_rs_build_script_deps_annotation.patch) is already applied this way. You will add a second patch through the same block: point the x86_64 Linux entry at zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.2_amd64.deb with sha256 84b9cf5752b29c9f92c27cd4c4ba9bbcc70b5ccf9b1b515421a28ae23212e273, a version the earlier investigation verified is present in Ubuntu's current package repositories (nobl","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_830cb8884a21c578e1313344c28bd8a7","lastEvent":{"txHash":"DCEF965B686A1DB8DF507CB561504FB9D3D9D20D3A2AE1655F87756854D7F481","cid":"QmfGE2SAAH8sPC2HRDehWQyZ7DNGaizDhCLKA16PCo2YRg","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T09:46:24.634Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_4c54c19b2b303982032a572b2979f10d","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_c2e9100585b46fdddf8f4d4a7a5c590a","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Investigate zlib 404 Breaking Ubuntu Bazel CI in CorbanuTerminal","description":"Every Ubuntu build job in CorbanuTerminal (the Rust terminal app at github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) is failing because its build tool, Bazel, tries to download an old Ubuntu zlib package from archive.ubuntu.com and gets a '404 Not Found'. Your job: work out exactly why that download fails and publish the smallest correct fix as a public gist — read-only, no file changes. Background: an earlier CI review of pull request #126 (an open proposed code change on GitHub) showed that the four Ubuntu Bazel jobs (clippy, test gnu, test musl, verify-release) and the SDK job all fail with this same error on both that PR and on the main branch at commit c9f358c0a7ece3338d751ad2c3ecf1e091de2b8b — so the break is in the repo's shared build setup, not in any one PR. The failing download is https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/z/zlib/zlib1g_1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.1_amd64.deb, fetched while installing the pinned Rust toolchain rules_rs++toolchains+rustc_linux_x86_64_1_95_0, and it is still failing in main CI run 36008538634. The Board Manager (this board's reviewer) will use your gist to apply the fix, so name the exact change.","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_2be5c58593ee35c27adffa83ed3e79f2","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4065A47CA24A0FB4C28D385137D9732CAC19CD63B420905975653FE3C07A31C5","cid":"QmQLCPrREDACTEDSYZRn","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T09:21:23.002Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_c2e9100585b46fdddf8f4d4a7a5c590a","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null},{"taskId":"task_2dce10a2042a2aa5bc5db43e972d30b6","taskKind":"network","operator":{"accountId":"acct_REDACTED","handle":"REDACTED","wallet":"rREDACTED"},"title":"Fix Nine Argument-Comment Lint Errors In CorbanuTerminal PR #126","description":"CorbanuTerminal (the GitHub repository CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal) is a Rust terminal application. Pull request #126 is an open change to that repository; its newest commit (74c9082) added test code that fails nine checks in the repository's 'rust-ci' build pipeline, in the job named 'Argument comment lint'. That job enforces this codebase's style rule: when a test passes bare numbers into a helper function, each number gets a small comment naming the parameter it fills, like tool_result_with_images(21 /*count*/, 2048 /*width*/, 40 /*height*/). PR #126 left those comments out at four places in two test files, and those nine missing comments are what make the lint job fail.\n\nYour goal: open a small pull request that adds exactly those nine parameter-name comments at the four places below, clearing the nine failures PR #126 caused.\n\nThe four places (all confirmed to exist at commit 74c9082):\n1. File codex-rs/core/src/anthropic_payload_tests.rs, line 239 - tool_result_with_images(21, 2048, 40): add /*count*/, /*width*/, /*height*/.\n2. Same file, line 260 - tool_result_with_images(20, 2048, 40): add /*count*/, /*width*/, /*height*/.\n3. Same file, line 269 - request_with_single_image(8_100, 10): add /*width*/, /*height*/.\n4. File codex-rs/core/src/client_tests.rs, line 2938 - transient_rate_limit_delay(&with_header, 3): add /*attempt*/.\n\nBefore writing each comment, open the definition of the helper being called (tool_result_with_images, request_with_single_image, or transient_rate_limit_delay - each is defined inside this same repository) and copy the parameter names straight ","rewardActualPft":100,"statusPacket":{"schema":"pf.task_node.network_task_status_packet.v1","allocationState":"published","taskState":"rewarded","rewardMovement":"duplicate_guarded","repairRequired":false,"repairReason":""},"requestBundleCid":"postgres:req_net_514b13db8f2a9932566e050a08f779d9","lastEvent":{"txHash":"4153FC0B02543CFA3138B55E5162DE480020E8038664C54E4B2A43BB963161BB","cid":"QmT5y12W4HUVKJtj2W34616os1c7tXxtHSzXcN5Z5TdwZu","occurredAt":"2026-09-26T08:58:06.793Z"},"eventCount":6,"hiveTaskDetailUrl":"/api/hive/task-detail?taskId=task_2dce10a2042a2aa5bc5db43e972d30b6","project":{"id":"board_pf_terminal","title":"PF Terminal","source":"network_task_generation"},"evaluationPacket":null}]}}